{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered","id":842010,"title":"Beasts overpowered? Try underpowered.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-04T11:14:31-08:00","id":842010,"title":"Beasts overpowered? Try underpowered.","content":"This started off as an aside in a werewolf thread where someone objected to how a Clash of Wills example made Beasts seem overpowered. Personally, I find it mind boggling that people consider Beasts to be that powerful. And here I'm going to examine why I consider Beast to be one of the less &quot;powerful&quot; of supernaturals. In the course of examination, I will be comparing the Begotten to vampires, werewolves, mages, and changelings. I won't be using Demon, given that the balancing feature of the Unchained are Compromises, making the effectiveness of the demons highly subjective. As well, I will be using the following areas of comparison, found primarily in the CofD core book:<br /> <br /> * Investigation / Tracking<br /> * Research<br /> * Social Maneuvering / Social Merits<br /> * Chases<br /> * Stealth<br /> * Crafting<br /> * Combat<br /> <br /> These five areas cover what I feel to be the overwhelming majority of situations that will come up in a game in some shape or another, and provides a wide basis of understanding situations where and how Beasts shine, and where they faulter.<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind that Beast, Mage, and Changeling, while we have enough information to do an analysis, aren't in a finalized edition yet. So, until I get a hard copy, some things may be subject to change.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Investigation / Tracking</u></b><br /> Five supernaturals all living together. The Beast has a mortal-but-psychic brother, whom the vampire was dating, the wolf adopted into the pack, changeling pledged, and the mage occasionally worked magic with him as a Sleepwalker. One day, this mortal died, brutally murdered. All five supernaturals rush to the scene of the crime.<br /> <br /> Vampires have access to Auspex 1, 2, and 3, all relevant for tracking. Vampires have a keen nose for blood as well. Further, there are a few notable Theban and Cruac divination rituals that can be used to outright point you in the direction of the killer. Call up an animal to help with tracking. Mehket have a 1 dot vision merit as well. There's a 4 dot Prophesy ritual that you could bribe a Theban Sorcerer to cast to simply magically force the killer to fall into your lap! Low level Cruac rituals provide even more visions and benefits.<br /> <br /> Werewolves can pick up the scent of the killer, and start tracking immediately. Impossible Spoor even lets them track a getaway car. Call up spirits for help. Lick blood under fingernails for tracking bonus, assuming defensive wounds. Knowledge Gifts are a thing as well.<br /> <br /> Mages? Information gathering is their forte. Anything the other supernaturals can do in terms of gathering info? A mage can do better. Post-cognition, asking spirits, following sympathetic connections between the dead body and the killer, scrying, Fate magic to create a fate of meeting once again.<br /> <br /> Changelings. Almost as flexible as mages. There are several post-cognition powers. You could create a custom Goblin Vow. In 1e, there was Oath and Punishment. Reflections of the Past Fairest aspect lets you name a specific person to scry on (the killer); hells, the various mirror magics let you scry on the killer, then step immediately out of a nearby reflection right next to them! Changeling hours could arguably rewind time and restore the mortal from death!<br /> <br /> Beasts. The problem with beasts is that, for the most part, Atavisms (Needs Must/Heart of the Ocean) that let you track only focus on 1) people you met before, or 2) something resonating with your Hunger in the immediate area. Nightmares can't track people, only manipulate them. So, the relevant abilities here are Mirmir\u2019s Wisdom, Needs Must and Direction Sense (advanced and epic). Mirmir's Wisdom seems pretty cool at first glance - Eidetic Memory, ehanced mental attributes, ability to tell lies, rote quality, Leverage, and temporary skill dots. The problem? All this is effectively mundane talent. Sure, you seem really good compared to a mortal. But, meanwhile, everyone else has already bypassed the need for doing things as a mortal. Mimir's Wisdom also lets you ask the ST a question to shed light on a subject. <i>However</i>, this question must be impersonal and cannot identify someone. Even Vampires can get visions that identify your mortal killers. Werewolves, mages, and changelings all have powers that do. The Beast cannot with Mimir's Wisdom. Which brings us to Needs Must / Heart of the Ocean. Needs Must, as said above, requires you to track someone you've already met in some way. You can also sense your Hunger fulfillment, but that not only relies on having an appropriate Hunger, but the killer to be nearby and no other options that will feed you. Lastly, there is Direction Sense. Advanced lets you track someone you've met before. Again. Still not helpful. Epic Direction Sense gives you post cognition. More helpful in knowing what happened, but still doesn't help you find your killer - you still haven't marked or directly sensed the killer, which all other abilities rely on.<br /> <br /> What does that leave us with? Beasts generally floundering at roughly a mortal pace. Generally speaking, Auspex and the Mehket Dream merit can do everything that Mimir's Wisdom and Direction Sense can when tracking an unknown person. And then, we have rituals that can do better. And vampires are generally the worst information gatherers of the early games. And all of this before we touch on the ability of mages and changelings to sense magic pretty much anywhere, giving them a huge leg up on any investigative tasks.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Research</u></b><br /> Research is important when trying to identify weaknesses of supernatural spiritual enemies - ephemerals, strix, etc. Even demons suffer from being researched.<br /> <br /> Mimir's Wisdom is pretty badass when it comes to doing research. Mental boost, access to libraries in your head, free questions. Vampires, Changelings and Mages, meanwhile, actually have the actual Libraries to do research - its a key part of their society. They can get the same rote quality and very likely teamwork to help. And that's not touching on their supernatural abilities. The sad state of affairs is that Mimir's Wisdom mainly replicates mundane skill and equipment that everyone else has access to. Sure, you are likely to be better than the others at gathering the same information a mortal can. But its not taking into account the numerous divination powers others have access to that give information raw research can't.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, lets look at Werewolves. They generally don't have Libraries - its not as important to their society like it is others. However, they don't need to do research - the Itheur is literally built to know everything that others need to research with their Aupsice abilities. Bane, ban, abilities, motives, drives? All Auspice powers. This does require a specific build, admittedly. But that's how the game is designed - you need to have a spread out pack to cover all threats.<br /> <br /> If we're talking doing research about physical opponents (ala Investigation rules), then again, we're looking at Mimir's Wisdom granting Leverage versus all the Auspice abilities, dream merit, Knowledge Gifts, divination Arcana, and various changeling divinations. One ability that works roughly at mortal speed versus supernatural insight that goes beyond the mortal is generally going to favor the supernatural insight. That one question of Mimir's Wisdom is pretty restrictive in a way no one else is.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Social Maneuvering / Merits</u></b><br /> I consider this to be two separate areas that are closely related, though they can often come with different builds. For example, take Werewolf. Cahalith and Irraka both have social maneuvering abilties, but the Elodoth has the power to manipulate social merits.<br /> <br /> So, lets talk about social merits first. Vampire is pretty much defined by having supernatural Status everywhere. The Invictus and Carthians specialize in favor trading to get more and more social merit abilities. Elodoth can manipulate them through their Gifts. Mages have their Mystery Cults that come with their Order Status, which I'm sure comes with some Allies and Contacts when we start looking at the GotV and SL. With Changeling, it depends on the Court - Spring did in the past, and I can't vouch for all the new ones having access to some magical way to manipulate social merits and be the whole spider thing. Even then, though, you generally can call upon the help of your fellow Court mates. Beasts, meanwhile? It just doesn't come up. Its not a thing at any point. Even social Tyrants have to progress up the ladder like a mortal. Admittedly a mortal with magical benefits, but still at mortal speed. The Begotten have no innate social support or ties beyond the brood. That leaves them at a disadvantage compared to everyone else. Not really that big of a surprise, though - Beast is basically the anti-Hunter game, and social support is one of the strengths of that game. Why else would Profession and Conspiracies be that huge of a thing?<br /> <br /> Anyways, moving on to Social Maneuvering. Now, Beasts are looking pretty good with Alien Allure, Siren's Trecherous Song, and You Must Obey. You can even use Nightmares to help when Forcing Doors. Alien Allure and Siren give massive massive dice pools; we're talking like 2x Lair + extra striking looks benefit + fake Status. On the surface, we're looking pretty good. That is until you realize that large dice pools are pretty meaningless when opening Doors normally. Exceptional success gives you an extra door. Woo! You can magically boost Impression up from average to Good to maybe even Excellent with all the merits and Atavisms.<br /> <br /> Vampires bypass the need to open Doors entirely with Majesty and Dominate. Mages can open all Doors with a simple Mind spell. Irraka and Cahalith both have ways of opening doors for free. Changelings' Mask of Superiority opens 3 doors automatically; that's twice as effective as a simple Exceptional Success. I know for a fact that vampires, werewolves, and mages have ways of creating Perfect Impressions magically for when you want a different approach; I don't see anything with Changeling at the moment, but I could be missing something. When it comes to Maneuvering, its really not the size that matters, its how you use it. Or, rather, how well you can manipulate Impressions and auto-opening Doors. Rolling one giant dice pool once an hour isn't nearly as good as rolling five times in a single minute with an average dice pool. And even then, both pale before simply opening all of a mark's Doors at once. Using regular methods, a Beast simply lacks the same ability that all other splats have for playing nice.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, Beasts do have a way of opening all doors at once. You Force them. In fact, the giant dice pool is very, very good for that. You even get an implied threat (and thus Hard Leverage) with the Satiety expendature of Alien Allure. Beasts are literally designed to excell at Forcing Doors. And sure, a Low Satiety AA can even repair damage the next day. That assumes that there is a next day, that your target hasn't become a Hero, and that your target hasn't used the burned bridges to sabotage you before that next day comes around. Which can very much be a problem, leaving enemies in your wake.<br /> <br /> Lets take a moment for looking at mind control. Nightmares, for the most part, all sort of control minds in some way. The problem is that a lot of them are combat abilities. Robbing your defense, direct damage, making someone run away in fear, inflicting poison. And the ones that aren't combat? Curses to make someone weaker in some way. Sure, that can make a target worse at socializing than you. But its not making you better. You can socially isolate someone unless they spend willpower, you can strip their Striking Looks, you can inflict penalties and Conditions. Which is good against a mortal, but doesn't stop another supernatural from using their above abilities to still be better at Social Maneuvering than you.<br /> <br /> You Must Obey is pretty much the signature mind control ability of the game. Which, unfortunately, is still highly restrictive. Compared to Dominate, you can't force someone to forget, you can't enforce complete compliance as they only operate out of fear, and once out of sight, they stop doign what you say. Dominate breaks when the target is struck, making it worthless in combat. YMO generally fails against threat of bodily harm or another Integrity breaking point. Vainglory and the Mind Arcana can rewrite people's memories as well as make them do things they normally wouldn't do. The Beast has nothing comparable. Werewolf lacks a lot of mind control powers, but they can craft fetishes that can have a lot of emotional manipulation and Urging someone to do things with spirits. Given everything, I'd say the two games are roughly comparable for last-place-on-mind-control.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Chases</b></u><br /> Under the new rules, Urhan werewolves flat out dominate chases. No if, and, or but about it. And there are ways to make a victim stop being chased as well as Gifts to further boost the innate superiority in Chases. That said, while I will maintain that werewolves are hands down the best here, Beasts are pretty good. Not only can they run pretty fast with Wings of the Raptor, but this is a situation where Nightmares are handy, assuming you have enough Satiety to use them. Or the target doesn't use magical abilities to teleport away. Khaibit vamps, changelings, and mages all have teleport abilities.<br /> <br /> In any case, the point is that this isn't actually an area where the Beasts are underpowered. However, considering they come in second to wolves, they definitely aren't overpowered either.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Stealth</b></u><br /> <i>Vampires</i> - Obfuscate, you can't see me! You don't notice me making sound or doing practically anything. You don't notice other people I make you ignore.<br /> <br /> <i>Werewolf</i> - super dice bonuses and rote quality against Clash of Wills. Sure, its mundane Stealth rolls, and you have to act stealthy, but there's so many bonuses that we're practically talking about assured success against anyone opposing you. Mages with Spirit Sight (rote quality to notice werewolves) are the only ones I'd give a chance of success, and that's pretty niche since they have to know to look in the first place. You can cross the Gauntlet for another method of stealth.<br /> <br /> <i>Mage</i> - take your pick of method. Creative Thaum at its best.<br /> <br /> <i>Changeling</i> - Phantom Glory, Light Shy, Nevertread... there's some very good methods here. Honestly, there's so many<br /> <br /> <i>Beast</i> - This is pretty bad, actually. There are two abilities - From the Shadows and Shadowed Soul. In the first case, its like Obfuscate lite. The Normal and Low Satiety are roughly equivalent to Obfuscate 1. Worse, because even passive magical senses break this with no contest. Passive mage sight, kenning, possibly even predator's aura. You have to spend Satiety to get the potential for Clash of Wills. And it breaks with an attack. Obfuscate 3 lets you pull others in to your magic to attack while still cloaked, blowing it out of the water. I don't think mage invisiblity is restricted to not attacking. Definitely one of the worst options.<br /> <br /> Now, as for Shadowed Soul. This is kind of cool. The normal ability lets you merge with shadows - no form to detect. You can listen through the shadows, and you can teleport to shadows. The problem is that you can't leave the shadows, or the effect ends. You can't do anything other than observe, or the effect ends. That's a very severe restriction. Its very telling that Beast, with spending two Satiety and using every potential stealth ability at their disposal, is arguably worse than a vampire with Obfuscate 1 and a certain devotion. And the vampire only gets better from there. And mages can pretty much do what a vampire can do with some preparation. Phantom Glory from Changeling can turn you into an undetectable ghost or gust of wind, and you can pull others into your state of being, just as vamps and mages can.<br /> <br /> I suppose a better comparison might be against Werewolf, who get an odd selection of abilities scattered between Human form, New Moon Gifts, Evasion Gifts, and Stealth Gifts. In short, Irraka are really good at blending into crowds, people not paying attention or remembering them, and crossing the gauntlet to spy/move in from there. Stealth Gifts are good at being hidden, making sure pack mates keep stealth as well. Evesion lets a wolf stick their nose back into hiding when someone does notice them, both physically and socially. They can ignore alarms and other technology when Beasts can't. Breaking down the From the Shadow abilities again, the Normal effect is like the human form &quot;can't pick me out!&quot; crowd effect. Low Satiey effect is like the Stealth Gift that gives Rote quality. Satiety Expendature is the only area where Beasts can do something that Werewolves can't do just as well - turn invisible. But the werewolf has a host of other stealthy abilities that let them blend in and, more importantly, be unremembered. Beasts don't want to be forgotten- they want to stand out boldly and inflict nightmares on people, because that feeds their Horror. Spying from the Shadow and from Shadowed Form seem roughly equivalent to me. Beasts can't make technology ignore them like a wolf can. Beasts can't bring others with them. So, the question becomes - who's better, wolf or beast, at hiding? Depends on how much you value pure invisibility.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Crafting</u></b><br /> Now, this is pretty simple. Neither Vampire nor Beast have magic items of the current 2e gamelines, while everyone else does. Niether have powers that give bonuses to working on mundane items, while everyone else does. Most 1e games did as well. And, even then? Vampire technically does get a few limited &quot;magic items&quot; that they can make through Theban / Cruac rituals, as well as arguably some Ordo stuff. Blessed weapons and gargoyles come immediately to mind, as does mandrake gardens and alchemical solutions. In terms of building mundane equipment, Vampire and Beast are roughly equal. Beast can buff up mental skills, and Vampire can beef up social and physical dice pools easily. Still, because of the magical equipment angle, I must give Vampire the advantage here, leaving BtP the worst when it comes to crafting in the whole of the CofD.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Combat</b></u><br /> Now, we come to the last category. Combat. There's several things we need to cover before we even talk in any depth about the matter. First, we need to assume that the Beast is going to have Low Satiety. Not only are the majority of combat powers Atavisms, and thus more effective, but High Satiety characters lose their Lair as a bonus to resist magical effects. That leaves them widely open to any sort of power to shut them down. While its possible to use combat Nightmares to good effect, its much more like a D&amp;D wizard - in other words, glass cannon combined with Save or Suck effects. Whomever goes first would win. Everyone has rocket-tag options. Except that most supernaturals aren't glass cannons like High Satiety Beasts.<br /> <br /> Next, lets touch on tactics. Lots of people also have insect-swarm forms, retainer / familar swarms, long ranged gunners, elemental magic control, and more. Combat is highly fluid situation where a wide variety of tactics, builds, styles, and more. There's two I want to focus on - front line warrior and magic user. Why? Because the former is actually rather notable for real life simulated situations - gladiators. There are competitions with both of them that can easily be translated to the CofD. At least for me - I am not shy about using the Midnight Games in my campaign. And the latter, because, well, magic. I'm not using a long range gunner option because 1) its heavily stealth and movement based, of which Beast really doesn't have any powers along that line, and 2) we already covered stealth.<br /> <br /> So, gladiator style. Daeva with Vigor 3, a Rahu with Purity 2, Glory 1, and a Giant with Cyclopean Strength and Limb From Limb (assume starting Satiety 5, and spend to immediately get Low Satiety and activate both Atavisms to fullest). Starting characters. Assume 3 in each relevant stat for simplicity, and Supernatural Resistance of 2.<br /> <br /> The Daeva and Rahu get to deal additional damage from their supernatural powers on top of their weapons / claws. The Daeva deals +3 damage on top of a +2 or +3 lethal weapon, plus riding the wave bonuses, plus spending vitae. The Rahu is dealing +4L between his Gifts and claw. With Lair 2, the Giant is dealing +4 damage with his claws as well, but as agg. The problem? While it seems that the agg dealing Giant is going to win, there's a small problem. Both the Daeva and Rahu are far better grapplers at this point of the game, getting at least +4 benefits. And the Giant needs the agg to bypass the vamp and wolf's innante healing. Meanwhile, the Rahu is getting +Purity dots to his health, meaning that he can soak at least one turn's worth of agg before establishing the grapple. And maintain it. Next turn? Efficent Killer for lots of damage. The Daeva is at more risk from the agg claws. However, with a fireaxe and Vigor, that's a minimum of 7 damage on the first turn with just one success; the daeva also has a better dice pool thanks to Vigor, averaging 3 successes with vitae and willpower, for a total of roughly 9 damage. The beast is only getting automatic successes, meaning that our base dice pool is going to be 3 + 3 - (defense of 6), so we need to spend willpower just to get a roll, and average 1 success. The vamp has enough to put down our giant, but not the giant our Daeva.<br /> <br /> I don't know how mages work, so they get a pass. Changelings? Interestingly, they don't have an option for getting more automatic successes on a hit. Not with the Contracts we see. Just a Strength (and other general dice) boost, armor boosts and Wyrd/2 unarmed attacks. Generally, you're better off with a +3L fire axe. Elegant Protection makes it harder to hit the Changeling, though. Meanwhile, the Giant gets auto successes, but few boosts to actual dice pools. If we're in a situation where we can't <i>hit </i>the changeling because of chance dice rolling, and the changeling can hit the Beast for small damage? Beast doesn't get mundane armor against a Render kith. As well, there's the Cloak of Elements - autodamage from being too close to the 'ling.<br /> <br /> Right now, I want to point out that it seems that everyone is beating the Beast in a gladiator style situation. How can that be? Beasts don't start with good innate abilities for combat. Vampires and werewolves, both supernatural predators, start with some very good abilities - healing, damage reduction, physical boosts. With Changeling, I get to start with a little bit of magical combat ability thanks to my choice of kith. Beasts get <i>no</i> supernatural combat ability outside Atavisms. Where Beasts have an advantage is that they are highly XP efficent. Changelings need to buy up Contract as well as Wyrd dots, vampires pick between several different Disciplines, werewolves raise up five Renown scores. Beasts just raise up Lair. Eventually, they will surpass a combat wolf or vamp because of this.<br /> <br /> Now, for magical strength. There's a couple of Nightmares that can be rather strong, but again, we're talking about being rather defenseless in the meantime. But where Beasts actually shine? Elemental magic. Between the immunities from the Lairs, actually calling down their Lairs to cause environmental damaging effects, and some Atavisms like Storm Lashed, there's some potent abilities that come on command. Vampires really kind of suck at this part, no pun intended. Werewolves have a few elemental Gifts, but I don't believe they have protection against the elements. Certainly not against lightning or ice. Changelings are just as competative as the Beasts, though they can't do city-wide storms. Mages can do spells, but that requires time and preparation, when Beasts do it naturally. Mass scale elemental powers and immunities is where Beasts really do excel at. But, then again? Massive scale effects generally are a Bad Idea. You don't want to raise a bunch of Heroes by being too flashy and scary. In a world that wants you to be hidden, flashy isn't the best option. YMMV, but I consider it a mark against them. Another mark is that, while they're good at elemental magic for combat, its less useful for beneficial uses of that same magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Satiety Issues</u></b><br /> When making these comparisons, I assumed that a Beast can always use their Satiety effects. That generally doesn't happen though, at least not in my experience. Satiety expendature is when crap hits the fan. Vampires can casually spend vitae, because its easy to replenish and plentiful. If they lose all of it, they just need to eat. Their abilities are stable throughout their entire track. Beasts rely on either being high Satiety (and thus fragile), or Low (and thus around Satiety 4, limiting their powerful abilities). Like, take the gladiator system. A vampire can easily replenish their vitae and fight on. Same with a werewolf and esssence and a changelign with their glamour. A Beast needs to devote an entire scene to feeding. And that brings them up to 4 or so. On a bad roll, less. Most vampire powers and werewolf Gifts I mentioned don't even require fuel, and they're a match for a notable number of Satiety effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Where Beasts Shine</b></u><br /> Its not all doom and gloom. Beasts, because of how Lair and Satiety are the only two big things you need to worry about, are extremely XP efficent. That means that, while other supernaturals rely on pack and society, each Beast is a walking jack-of-all-trades. They're good at a wide variety of subjects and abilities. This makes them extremely flexible. How else would they jump from a vampire party, to help a mage chase their Obsession, to hanging out with a werewolf on the Hunt? Beasts don't specialize as well as other splats do. Or, at least not when it comes to the above areas of the game I mentioned.<br /> <br /> Beasts also have a tendacy to collect Immunities like candy. Environmental Tilts, personal combat Tilts, etc.<br /> <br /> Beast: the Primordial isn't a Social, Physical, or Mental game. Its not a game of Second Chances, about Madness, or about Stolen Lives. Its a game about dabbling in all of that. Jack of All Trades, Master of None. You are never going to be a better socialite than an Invictus Ventrue, a better hunter than a werewolf, or a better investigator than a mage. But you can hold your own, and if being a workable <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/JackOfAllStats?from=Main.TheMario\" target=\"_blank\">Mario</a> is overpowered? That's one thing. But, given that what prompted this little rant was people saying that Beasts outshone other supernaturals in the field that supernatural is supposed to specialize in? I have no reason to believe that, and every reason to disagree.<br /> <br /> High Lair Beasts are still scary, because you are never sure what their weakness is. If any - Anathema are unpredictable without a Hero. And the Lair means that there's a good chance that the Beast has access to whatever weakness you have. There's a good chance of a wide variety of defenses, and they can hurt striking back in a wide variety of measures. But, unlike any other supernatural, you can't nail down what their flaws are. Where you can exploit them. And that's the scary part. Well, that, and the fact that they come built in with lots of fear powers. But there are sharp limits to what they can know and do. And those restrictions are what make me feel that Beasts aren't even close to overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-04-2016, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T11:36:16-08:00","id":842027,"title":"","content":"The full quote? Jack of all trades, master of none,though oftentimes better than master of one.<br /> <br /> That's their deal. I had to deal with regenerating. swarming Namratu immune to being blinded, or limb-wracked, who could virtually teleport hundreds of feet without penalties, and the only plausible way to do it was to immolate a small town with Cataclysm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T12:25:10-08:00","id":842069,"title":"","content":"What makes Beasts even scarier, in my opinion, at mostly at High Satiety, is how they clearly incentivize all these specialists to come together, providing an undeniably amazing safe-place that can help increase mobility in several ways, skew the environments to their advantage, strengthen them, front-run for them, etc. Beasts provide a great platform for everyone else to stand on and shine with, and in doing so provides himself a retinue of exceptional skill.<br /> <br /> There's a reason I tend towards the Lord of the Castle/Master of Monsters angle of Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T12:41:21-08:00","id":842083,"title":"","content":"Oh, Beasts are amazing at what they do. I just kind of went on a rant because I got a bit tired of hearing people say that beasts are overpowered. They're no more overpowered than any other splat in the CofD. Meaning, they're mainstream in terms of ability. I kinda went overboard, I guess. They don't outshine the predators at being predators. They don't outshine mages at magic, nor the fae at trickery. And that's exactly what people were saying happened. It doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T12:52:02-08:00","id":842090,"title":"","content":"I think the main advantage of Beasts is their immunities. Having a specific Lair Trait makes you immune to that particular, potentially harmful, thing. It's easy enough to find fireproof Eshmaki who can't ever be blinded just from two of their in-Family Atavisms. Factor in Lair Traits, and a Beast could easily find themselves immune to poison, disease, drowning, being trapped, becoming lost, etc. The 'being trapped' bit I'm extrapolating from Closed Exits being a Lair Trait- if a Beast is immune to their Lair Traits, then the logical immunity to Closed Exits is <i>always </i>having a way out.<br /> <br /> Then, there's Primordial Pathways, which allows them to world hop fairly easily. Let's see your average Werewolf follow the Begotten into the Astral Realms or the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T12:53:30-08:00","id":842093,"title":"","content":"Yeah, overpowered isn't how I would describe Beasts.<br /> <br /> I spend most of my time trying to think about how organized societies of Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, and Changelings don't just pwn them out of existence. All I can really ever come up with that Beasts sharing kinship with any of these 4 supernaturals frequently end up as pets (unless the Beasts diversify their Kin and then strategically play them off against one another, which seems like it'll end poorly for all involved). I wish the word count for Beast had been longer as the crossover play section could have been much beefier. Hopefully the StG will include many more words / much more advice on how best to cross the streams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T13:01:32-08:00","id":842105,"title":"","content":"Also- Beasts can run and hide in a place <i>no one else </i>can reach, and relax until it's relatively safe to come out. In regards to why Changelings specifically don't wipe out Beasts, I could see it as Beasts being monumentally useful to Changelings. Another dreamwalker without the vulnerabilities of Frailties that understands the importance of myths and legends who can warp the Hedge and- with sufficient power -potentially stand toe to toe with the Gentry? Sounds like it's better to have the dragon in your camp facing out than outside the camp facing in.<br /> <br /> And can you imagine how useful a Beast with the Maze Lair Trait would be in the Hedge? They would never get lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T14:14:27-08:00","id":842145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842105#post842105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also- Beasts can run and hide in a place <i>no one else </i>can reach, and relax until it's relatively safe to come out. In regards to why Changelings specifically don't wipe out Beasts, I could see it as Beasts being monumentally useful to Changelings. Another dreamwalker without the vulnerabilities of Frailties that understands the importance of myths and legends who can warp the Hedge and- with sufficient power -potentially stand toe to toe with the Gentry? Sounds like it's better to have the dragon in your camp facing out than outside the camp facing in.<br /> <br /> And can you imagine how useful a Beast with the Maze Lair Trait would be in the Hedge? They would never get lost.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds like a pet to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T14:17:08-08:00","id":842149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842069#post842069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes Beasts even scarier, in my opinion, at mostly at High Satiety, is how they clearly incentivize all these specialists to come together, providing an undeniably amazing safe-place that can help increase mobility in several ways, skew the environments to their advantage, strengthen them, front-run for them, etc. Beasts provide a great platform for everyone else to stand on and shine with, and in doing so provides himself a retinue of exceptional skill.<br /> <br /> There's a reason I tend towards the Lord of the Castle/Master of Monsters angle of Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, my reaction to the hypothetical example OP used in the first post was basically &quot;forget about mechanics, that sounds like the greatest sitcom ever, I totally want to know more about who these monsters are and where they live&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T14:35:16-08:00","id":842164,"title":"","content":"I could also go for monsters sitcocm. Hell, I almost do it-most of my games tend toward the slice of life angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T15:03:33-08:00","id":842177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842145#post842145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a pet to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like putting things in really diminishing and insulting terms because of a pre-existing bias against the logical ease with which the Begotten engage with other supernaturals and are able to get along or serve as useful allies if they care to. Also, the other splats have no more reasons to want to eliminate them as a whole than they do for each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-04-2016, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T15:12:03-08:00","id":842180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842177#post842177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like putting things in really diminishing and insulting terms because of a pre-existing bias against the logical ease with which the Begotten engage with other supernaturals and are able to get along or serve as useful allies if they care to. That, and the other splats have no more reason to want to eliminate them as a whole than they do for each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>No reason to make it personal.<br /> <br /> I'm all about logical consequences. If you can formulate a logical argument for why a Vampire wouldn't blood bond a Beast, a pack of Werewolves physically dominate into a specific spot on the pack pecking order, Mages do any number of things, or Changelings (who are some of the most suspicious creatures out there) to get it to sign a contract then I might be inclined to think it's not a problem. But the fact is that these are all secretive, violent societies and they don't suffer new factors lightly. Think it through. It can't possibly be all roses and chocolates when your kin can Lash Out at you, etc., etc.<br /> <br /> YMMV. But in my games Beasts dealing with the Big 4 are most likely going to end up as pets. That's just a reality of the social dynamics their inserting themselves into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T15:30:15-08:00","id":842186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842180#post842180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No reason to make it personal.<br /> <br /> I'm all about logical consequences. If you can formulate a logical argument for why a Vampire wouldn't blood bond a Beast, a pack of Werewolves physically dominate into a specific spot on the pack pecking order, Mages do any number of things, or Changelings (who are some of the most suspicious creatures out there) to get it to sign a contract then I might be inclined to think it's not a problem. But the fact is that these are all secretive, violent societies and they don't suffer new factors lightly. Think it through. It can't possibly be all roses and chocolates when your kin can Lash Out at you, etc., etc.<br /> <br /> YMMV. But in my games Beasts dealing with the Big 4 are most likely going to end up as pets. That's just a reality of the social dynamics their inserting themselves into.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is until a beast incarnates in which case I am pretty sure it changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T15:37:51-08:00","id":842189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842180#post842180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can formulate a logical argument for why a Vampire wouldn't blood bond a Beast, a pack of Werewolves physically dominate into a specific spot on the pack pecking order, Mages do any number of things, or Changelings (who are some of the most suspicious creatures out there) to get it to sign a contract then I might be inclined to think it's not a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Because</i> why would a Vampire by default try to blood bond a Beast that is seeking to work with them in a mutually beneficial way or act towards a positive relationship, especially when having it exposed would turn it sour more often than not, and vampires really ought to be more cautious than that; <i>Because</i> why would Werewolves do that to a Beast who has no quarrel with them or becomes a part of the pack peacefully anymore than they would do it to a new Wolf-Blooded or Uratha; <i>Because</i> that paints a really reductive and very unWise picture of Mages as a whole and you might as well be asking &quot;why wouldn't they do any of this number of things to every other supernatural thing in the world they come across or even each other&quot;; And because, geez, maybe it's just not convenient to sign a contract with every single person you're suspicious of, especially when the circumstances might allow for some measure of trust to be developed without the need for one? That said, yes a Changeling might very likely Seal one of the Beasts's statements, just as they're likely to do with a new Changeling they don't know, but if the Beast is actually amicable nothing untoward seems likely to come from it. I don't see how something Changelings often lean on to establish bars of cooperation or trust is going to bring down Beasts to the status of <i>pets</i>, especially given how powerful they <i>can </i>be. You're not making an even argument with Changelings or with Mages.<br /> <br /> Of course it's not going all going to be roses. But going to the opposite end and claiming it's all going to be thorns is, in my opinion, extremely disingenuous. Of course, I'm not going to tell you how to play your games. If your supernaturals are all as callous as to have the outcomes you describe be the default state of things at their best, okay. But I wouldn't say it's an accurate representation of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-04-2016, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T15:51:29-08:00","id":842199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842189#post842189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Because</i> why would a Vampire by default try to blood bond a Beast that is seeking to work with them in a mutually beneficial way or act towards a positive relationship, especially when having it exposed would turn it sour more often than not, and vampires really ought to be more cautious than that; <i>Because</i> why would Werewolves do that to a Beast who has no quarrel with them or becomes a part of the pack peacefully anymore than they would do it to a new Wolf-Blooded or Uratha; <i>Because</i> that paints a really reductive and very unWise picture of Mages as a whole and you might as well be asking &quot;why wouldn't they do any of this number of things to every other supernatural thing in the world they come across or even each other&quot;; And because, geez, maybe it's just not convenient to sign a contract with every single person you're suspicious of, especially when the circumstances might allow for some measure of trust to be developed without the need for one? That said, yes a Changeling might very likely Seal one of the Beasts's statements, just as they're likely to do with a new Changeling they don't know, but if the Beast is actually amicable nothing untoward seems likely to come from it. I don't see how something Changelings often lean on to establish bars of cooperatio or trust is going to bring down Beasts to the status of <i>pets</i>, especially given how powerful they <i>can </i>be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't you want to Blood Bond a Beast if you were a Vampire. For that matter if your a Vampire why wouldn't you try to Blood Bond everyone you could. Mind control, it's a Vampire's friend.<br /> <br /> Packs have pecking orders. No pack is going to have a Beast as an Alpha.<br /> <br /> etc., etc.<br /> <br /> Sorry if you think that's messed up but it's all pretty logical to me as I look at the big picture of how all these things fit together. (And it's a great driver of plot in games. Power vacuums exist to be filled.) YMMV but that hardly means I'm being disingenuous. My position is as valid as anyone else's. For best results Beasts probably want to team-up with each other or team-up with rarer supernaturals like Prometheans, Mummies, Deviants, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T15:53:01-08:00","id":842201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842186#post842186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is until a beast incarnates in which case I am pretty sure it changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't actually have enough rules to really know what this means. (IIRC, Heroes might be some kind of necessary factor.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T15:57:29-08:00","id":842205,"title":"","content":"Packs don't really have pecking orders in the way you're saying they do. Not usally anyhow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T16:00:18-08:00","id":842209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842199#post842199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Packs have pecking orders. No pack is going to have a Beast as an Alpha.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, this is not a guarantee in 2nd Ed, it's mentioned that some packs do this, but not all.<br /> <br /> More generally, it seems like you are generalizing pretty hard, and if that's how you play that's fine, but not every Vampire wants to Blond Bond the whole world in the default setting. Same goes for the other splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T16:06:44-08:00","id":842213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't you want to Blood Bond a Beast if you were a Vampire. For that matter if your a Vampire why wouldn't you try to Blood Bond everyone you could. Mind control, it's a Vampire's friend.</div> </div> </div> </div> A couple reasons off the top of my head:<br /> \u2022Because they believe it is morally wrong.<br /> \u2022Because they fear that doing so is dangerous to their Humanity.<br /> \u2022They believe that other Kindred would construe it as a threat or otherwise have an agressive reaction.<br /> \u2022They feel the risk of inducing Vitae Addiction or the unhinged behaviors associated with high-level Blood Bonds in that many people is an unacceptable risk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Packs have pecking orders. No pack is going to have a Beast as an Alpha.</div> </div> </div> </div> True, though I don't believe Alphas are a inherent thing anymore, but that doesn't need mean that they're at the bottom of the rung*, and even then, I think most Packs would be smart enough to not treat the bottom rung that bad.<br /> <br /> *Especially since one with the right Atavisms and Satiety to spend might have well been packing silver, and one at high Satiety could serve as a useful negotiator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T16:31:31-08:00","id":842227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842199#post842199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Packs have pecking orders. No pack is going to have a Beast as an Alpha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends strongly on the Beast in question, their relative power and ability to charm or force the werewolves to kowtow.<br /> <br /> In social and combat applications particularly, MCN's rant is really strongly biased against the Beast player understanding their own Template - for example the implication that you should start at low Satiety to win a fight, rather than starting at high Satiety, pop your favorite &quot;GLHF&quot; Nightmares while setting up Lair traits, and then chunk yourself down to low Satiety by spamming Atavism effects. It requires a little setup, but Beasts have incredibly strong defensive tools - you can kite into and out of shadows and heal your whole bar back while you're doing this stuff. In an actual play situation it can go either way - almost always, for almost everyone, even a Demon isn't in good shape if the fight starts with an Obfuscated shotgun blast to the back of the head - but both in terms of ability to brute-force social encounters (you know, the social thing that actually matters - they can force doors super-well and they have mind control, that they're only &quot;really good&quot; at playing nice with their supercharged Striking Looks and assorted bonuses isn't exactly important) and win out in serious fights Beasts are certainly powerful contenders, and they are unquestionably top picks for the 5-25xp range.<br /> <br /> Pretty much every other area is...skewed at best, but those two stand out.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call them jacks of all trades. More like experts of all trades, with some options for mastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","user":"Kingdom of One","date":". 03-04-2016, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:32:11-08:00","id":842277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842149#post842149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, my reaction to the hypothetical example OP used in the first post was basically &quot;forget about mechanics, that sounds like the greatest sitcom ever, I totally want to know more about who these monsters are and where they live&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Portland. Its a thing in my personal game. Not the mortal dying, but the group living together? We have two changelings, a vamp, three mages, and two wolves, and one psychic vampire template. <br /> <br /> I draw heavily from personal experience in my things I post here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:54:13-08:00","id":842293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842227#post842227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In social and combat applications particularly, MCN's rant is really strongly biased against the Beast player understanding their own Template</div> </div> </div> </div> And you seem to be not reading what I actually wrote. I firmly established a gladiator game with starting PCs as the comparison of strength. Your little kiter character is not a starting PC, nor operating in a gladitorial setting. I admitted that the Beasts were good at Forcing Doors, but explained the problems of only being good at Forcing Doors, and how virtually everyone else had better, non offensive methods of opening doors that weren't aggressive or threatening. If you are going to call my statements biased, at least do me the courtesy of actually using what I said and the context I use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T18:13:04-08:00","id":842307,"title":"","content":"Beasts don't start out the strongest at melee combat, but they scale faster than almost anyone else. Except, oddly, in the case of Armor. Beasts have better out the gate armor than almost anything other than Metalflesh, but it doesn't scale with Lair. They have crazy potent poison in Basilisk's touch, too, though Toxicity mechanics make it vastly more potent applied out of combat than in.<br /> <br /> As for Social, Forcing Doors only leads to problems if you fail, and that's unlikely to happen with someone stacking Alien Allure, Striking Looks, and Siren's Treacherous Song. <br /> <br /> Also, we do have mechanics for Incarnate Beasts, and they are incredibly powerful. They get [Lair] special abilities from a list, so at least 8, which includes nifty abilities like adding Lair to Strength and Armor. An Incarnate Beast is entirely capable of having enough armor that Thermite won't even damage them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T18:24:02-08:00","id":842315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered#post842010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not all doom and gloom. Beasts, because of how Lair and Satiety are the only two big things you need to worry about, are extremely XP efficent. That means that, while other supernaturals rely on pack and society, each Beast is a walking jack-of-all-trades. They're good at a wide variety of subjects and abilities. This makes them extremely flexible. How else would they jump from a vampire party, to help a mage chase their Obsession, to hanging out with a werewolf on the Hunt? Beasts don't specialize as well as other splats do. Or, at least not when it comes to the above areas of the game I mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a complementary point to this aspect, growing in Lair also strongly encourages Beasts to spend a lot of those Experiences they're saving on Attributes \u2014 not only do your Resistance Traits set your Clash of Wills pool and further incentivize your family to stick close if they expect to be dealing with hostile magic, but once you hit Lair 6+ you've reached the point where Satiety isn't the deciding factor in how many dice you roll for a specializing subclass of Nightmares. (And that's to say nothing of the benefits to your Horror in general.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T18:34:20-08:00","id":842320,"title":"","content":"I think the observation leans a little heavily on personal experience that doesn't necessarily fit the games of others. Primarily in the Satiety Expenditure part. Expending Satiety really lets you overcome most of the drawbacks to the powers you've described, which, in Kingdom of One's defense, does make the statement seem biased. The focus is on pointing out weaknesses in these Atavisms, and instead of appreciating that you can expend Satiety to get over those weaknesses, dismiss Satiety Expenditure as something that 'generally doesn't happen.'<br /> <br /> That said, I've come to not believe in cross-splat balance so I don't agree with the idea that they're overpowered. Powerful, sure, but that's an aspect of every game so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T22:16:14-08:00","id":842411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842293#post842293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And you seem to be not reading what I actually wrote. I firmly established a gladiator game with starting PCs as the comparison of strength. Your little kiter character is not a starting PC, nor operating in a gladitorial setting. I admitted that the Beasts were good at Forcing Doors, but explained the problems of only being good at Forcing Doors, and how virtually everyone else had better, non offensive methods of opening doors that weren't aggressive or threatening. If you are going to call my statements biased, at least do me the courtesy of actually using what I said and the context I use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you tone that down like eighty degrees, maybe? I'm not saying every single thing you said is invalid, and I respect and acknowledge your right to rant and vent. I just don't think your conclusions or some of the premises you used to get to them are really accurate. I also don't think Beasts are really overpowered per se, in part because they're meant to murder (or overpower in various other ways short of murder) mortals and maybe each other and being phenomenally good at that is not flawed design, and in part because their role as a crossover entity benefits from them being extremely potent in ways other splats have a hard time dealing with - it's easier to accept a den mother than a tagalong, and Beasts are nobody's tagalong. They're as powerful as they're supposed to be. Balance between lines isn't exactly a developer priority in the first place.<br /> <br /> Socially, you pan Beasts for having no supernatural Social merits, but they have access to all the regular ones - which is all they NEED - and superpowered Striking Looks, which is *amazing* especially since SL isn't just a seduction thing. Sure, they don't have Merits-into-Merits-into-Merits like vampires - except they kinda do, since they can still take Mystery Cult Initiation, which does that for you if that's something you care about. But it's just...it's a lack that isn't felt. It's not like they're hurting here, really, you know?<br /> <br /> Then some stuff about Social Maneuvering, which is the worst way to social anyone. You right away imply Beasts are deficient and your example includes mind control powers from other lines, ignoring You Must Obey, which is the best of Dominate in a neat one-Nightmare package. What else you do need?! Mask of Superiority? Look, give me You Must Obey every TIME. Certainly from character creation Beasts are better than a Ventrue, because they still have another Nightmare free for whatever social effect they like (assuming the Ventrue goes for Dominate 3) and can sink their Atavisms into the Makara snuggle game. Definitely than a Daeva, Majesty doesn't get its wow factor until 4. For sure better than Werewolves. Not better than a Mastigos, granted, not better than a Demon, who are really really good at social things. Probably than a Changeling - well, that one's more variable. I'd rather have You Must Obey than Pledges sometimes, but that's really different KINDS of gameplay, you know? If you're measuring ability to accomplish ends, Beasts win it, but Pledges aren't really trying to do that in the first place, they're part of an aesthetic and conceptual space unique to Changeling. But Beasts &quot;lack the ability...&quot; when they literally have the same kind of power you're defining as &quot;the ability,&quot; something that ignores Doors! That's your criteria for Ventrue, it's not EVEN your criteria for character creation Daeva, why is it not enough for Beasts to get mentioned? You see what I mean?<br /> <br /> THEN we get to Forcing Doors. You admit Beasts are amazing at and then...write it off on the basis that your target might kill or sabotage you, or for some reason, spontaneously transform into a hero, over the course of one night. I can't imagine the gamestate where any of that happens. Even SABOTAGE, really, is way too extreme. Forcing Doors is just bringing bluntness to a conversation, it doesn't even necessarily engender hostility, it doesn't turn the security guard into your eight-hour nemesis. It probably makes the security guard not want to be your friend, but it doesn't even stop you from Forcing Doors again if you need to. Saying it's an always dangerous option is just a huge misrepresentation. Forcing Doors is super-useful and oftentimes is the best way to deal with a social situation where you need someone to do X and don't happen to have a week before X comes due. Plus you have an ability that resets the reaction to you Forcing Doors! That is very often enough to remove the disadvantage entirely. Most people don't in one day ruin your life because you were mean or demanding or blunt with them. Most people COULDN'T, but probably just WON'T - burning bridges isn't the same as earning an oath of vengeance.<br /> <br /> Finally you remember Nightmares and describe them in the most bizarre possible writeoff, like...you like this game, right? We both like it? Nightmares are AWESOME. Forcing someone to flee isn't a combat-restricted ability, and crippling people socially isn't irrelevant to how effective you are socially any more than inflicting Wrack tilts isn't irrelevant to your shot at winning a fight. Everything You Do Is Worthless is brutal. You Are Not Alone and You Will Never Rest both have amazing high-end effects that are even more effective situationally than You Must Obey. Then you imply that none of these crazy-powerful things is good against a supernatural because they still have their own powers - which you can defend against, same as they can try to defend against you, and which anyone who fails their defense is probably out of the contest...that's not a &quot;Beasts are worse-off&quot; situation. You slam a Fairest or a Mastigos with You Must Obey, you're good to go.<br /> <br /> Then you off-hand mention You Must Obey AT LAST and you're just like &quot;it's like bad Dominate,&quot; but the ways in which it's &quot;bad&quot; compared to the Ventrue with three dots aren't really a big deal, it DOESN'T end when they're out of your sight, and while you might not have &quot;complete compliance&quot; you're not exactly hurting for complex queued commands on a Satiety 8 invocation, so I'm not sure how relevant that really is. Just queue their last couple commands to come and find you for new orders, and to wait quietly once they've found you. You try to compare it to Werewolf WHILE ACKNOWLEDGING that Werewolf has no actual mind control! How is that a tie?! In ANY WAY, how is that a tie?!<br /> <br /> Every section is like that. It's all half-truths and smoke and mirrors and deliberate devaluation...there's another &quot;tied with Werewolves&quot; thing you do in Stealth, about how it depends &quot;how you value pure invisibility.&quot; PURE INVISIBILITY IS PRETTY VALUABLE.<br /> <br /> Beasts aren't overpowered, but they are very cool, and all this stuff you said about them is just off the mark. Again, I get that you were angry and expressing something, but you don't have to tear down the line to get that sentiment across, and I don't think it was accurate. Yes, there are ways in which Beasts lack, but none of those ways are social or combat from character creation. And most of your other categories have a fair amount of skew as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","user":"Kingdom of One","date":". 03-05-2016, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T04:41:56-08:00","id":842482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842411#post842411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ignoring You Must Obey, which is the best of Dominate in a neat one-Nightmare package.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have time to answer the whole post, sorry if I seem to be cherry picking. But i strongly disagree with this, You Must Obey easily being among the worst Dominate-alike out of any splat.<br /> It requires heavy babysitting of those you dominate, only lasts a scene, is limited on the number of orders you can give and orders can be ignored with a breaking point roll.<br /> <br /> Edit: also raises the question how it works against other supernaturals that don't have Integrity and Breaking Points. Probably not well. In a discussion on another forum about blood bond a designer mentioned that acting against a Blood bond is a breaking point towards 5 for Werewolf as they act against an imbalance inside themselves. So if the same is true for You Must Obey you may end up doing them a favour by allowing them to act against your orders, and &quot;You slam a Fairest or a Mastigos with You Must Obey, you're good to go.&quot; may end up the opposite as you wasted an action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 03-05-2016, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T04:54:24-08:00","id":842486,"title":"","content":"EDIT - nevermind. *deep breath*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-05-2016, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T05:42:50-08:00","id":842498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842307#post842307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts don't start out the strongest at melee combat, but they scale faster than almost anyone else. Except, oddly, in the case of Armor. Beasts have better out the gate armor than almost anything other than Metalflesh, but it doesn't scale with Lair. They have crazy potent poison in Basilisk's touch, too, though Toxicity mechanics make it vastly more potent applied out of combat than in.</div> </div> </div> </div> True. The scaling was something I meant to mention, but I think I forgot. Point for point, Gifts and Disciplines are at least equal, but better. The XP efficency means that you can invest more in things, faster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Social, Forcing Doors only leads to problems if you fail, and that's unlikely to happen with someone stacking Alien Allure, Striking Looks, and Siren's Treacherous Song. </div> </div> </div> There's a lot more context behind this than I went into with that initial post. Social maneuvering with supernaturals is how Beasts develop Kinship. Sure, against mortals, its easy enough to just Force Doors. You generally don't care about long term relationships with these people. However? Arcane had the right of it when he described Besats as the whole Mistress of Monsters. There are long term implications of using Forced Doors here on your minions. Sorry, I mean Kin. Sabotage can come in the form of merely disgruntled whispers that build up. Or, remember that at High Satiety, you actually can't add Lair to resist supernatural powers. So, if someone interrupts your Forcing Doors with a dominance play of their own? Both vampires and werewolves are predators used to such dominance play, and are known to respond in kind. And you can't tell me that a good portion of other supernaturals won't drool at taking over as the hub of this little gathering?<br /> <br /> Also, there's the fact that Forcing Doors tends to require coersion of some kind. Even if its only the implicit &quot;I am your boss, you must obey me!&quot; kind. How many people are comfortable using coersion as their modus operandus? It requires a special kind of mind to happily rely on it.<br /> <br /> And, interestingly, its actually is ineffective in the long run to not spend the time using Social Maneuvering. Low Satiety Alien Allure can give Persistant Charm Condition if you <i>don't</i> use Forcing Doors. Which means not only do you have Kin less likely to be subtly undermining you, but they're actually happily including you in their hunts, which means more Satiety. Meanwhile, if you Force Doors to make a Kin, word is likely going to spread through supernatural society, which actively hurts you.<br /> <br /> And, yeah, Heroes are still an issue. When you use that much supernatural charm to Force Doors, it can cause a trigger. So can feeding your Hunger. Any time you are obvious with your abilities (ie being blunt) there's a chance that you could attract a Hero. Heroes are the reason that Beasts generally don't live out in the open and need to stay hidden. It won't happen every time, but keep on rolling the dice and you will eventually hit snake eyes.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Forcing Doors isn't a cure-all for Beasts. In a pinch, its fine. But it has long term implications. No one exists in a vaccuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-05-2016, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T06:19:22-08:00","id":842511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842482#post842482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: also raises the question how it works against other supernaturals that don't have Integrity and Breaking Points. Probably not well. In a discussion on another forum about blood bond a designer mentioned that acting against a Blood bond is a breaking point towards 5 for Werewolf as they act against an imbalance inside themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it was a freelancer, not a developer. There were two or three writers in the particular thread, all of them with different takes, none of them official. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T06:27:21-08:00","id":842519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842511#post842511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it was a freelancer, not a developer. There were two or three writers in the particular thread, all of them with different takes, none of them official.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two, each with one take, each on one splat. Chris Allen on Werewolves vs Blood Bond and Dave Brookshaw on Mages and Blood Bond.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T06:28:39-08:00","id":842521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842205#post842205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Packs don't really have pecking orders in the way you're saying they do. Not usally anyhow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Weird. Pretty sure someone's the alpha. Pretty sure it isn't a Wolf-Blooded or a Human. Pretty sure it isn't going to be the Beast either. Werewolf isn't furry D&amp;D (despite the character class analogue of auspices).<br /> <br /> YMMV but I think you're missing the part where Werewolves are pretty much as Darwinian as the Spirits they hunt. All CofD game lines are in their heart of hearts games of <i><b>personal horror</b></i>. Without that aspect to the game you might as well be playing furry superheroes. If you're going to play superheroes then you might as well play Champions (or any number of other RPGs that a specifically focused on superheroes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T06:41:44-08:00","id":842527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842209#post842209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, this is not a guarantee in 2nd Ed, it's mentioned that some packs do this, but not all.<br /> <br /> More generally, it seems like you are generalizing pretty hard, and if that's how you play that's fine, but not every Vampire wants to Blond Bond the whole world in the default setting. Same goes for the other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You pretty much have to generalize pretty hard when you look at the big picture for setting. If I didn't generalize I'd never be able to develop plot for casts of thousands (afterall, I'm not going to write up thousands of individual supernaturals). I have to consider their actions in aggregate. What kind of world do they share? Very few NPCs are going to be exceptions to the generalizations, that's what the PCs are for.<br /> <br /> This would be kind of moot if Beasts had an ability like Vampires and Werewolves that lets them tell other predators that they're predators on equal footing and not worth the trouble of effing with. Similarly they lack any of the tricks that Mages and Changelings have that also amount to 'don't eat me dude, I can make you sorry for it.' Beasts are exactly like Remora. And while Remora have a relatively symbiotic relationship with sharks, they're still little fish and sharks do occasionally eat them.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Beasts are a bit under powered. They could use an ability sorta like a Demon's spoofing ability that let's them either remain under the radar or makes them look like too much trouble to eat. Alternately they could use some kind of metaphysical bargain ability that formalizes the Kinship relationship and places the burden of protecting them from other sharks on the shark they share kinship with. Said shark would need an additional incentive.<br /> <br /> This has been a good discussion. I've an idea for several hacks that can level the playing field and smooth cross-over play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T07:11:41-08:00","id":842543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842213#post842213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A couple reasons off the top of my head:<br /> \u2022Because they believe it is morally wrong.<br /> \u2022Because they fear that doing so is dangerous to their Humanity.<br /> \u2022They believe that other Kindred would construe it as a threat or otherwise have an agressive reaction.<br /> \u2022They feel the risk of inducing Vitae Addiction or the unhinged behaviors associated with high-level Blood Bonds in that many people is an unacceptable risk.<br /> <br /> True, though I don't believe Alphas are a inherent thing anymore, but that doesn't need mean that they're at the bottom of the rung*, and even then, I think most Packs would be smart enough to not treat the bottom rung that bad.<br /> <br /> *Especially since one with the right Atavisms and Satiety to spend might have well been packing silver, and one at high Satiety could serve as a useful negotiator.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I apologize if you find this insulting. That is not my intention. We fundamentally disagree on Vampires and likely on CofD games in general.<br /> Points 1 and 2 are just silly. Vampires are monsters. They might be protagonists but in no world are they heroes. Morality isn't a thing in CofD games and asking them not to use Blood Bonds is effectively asking them to walk around with one arm tied around their back. Never forget, Vampires are blood-sucking predators that hunt humans for food. <br /> <br /> Despite appearances to the contrary, Humanity 4~6 is the best level to maintain.<br /> <br /> Regarding point 3, I'm not sure I follow. The entire Lashing Out section provides rules for Vampires to assert dominance over one another without resorting to physical violence.<br /> <br /> Point 4, is also silly. Ghouls go through life Blood Bonded. Many Childer are also likely to. Blood addiction is a core theme to the game afterall.<br /> <br /> Regarding packs and treatment, think of the Darwinian nature of the game, take a look at actual wolves in nature, look again at the inspirational material for W:tF, and especially, watch Sons of Anarchy. How the players play Werewolves is one thing but generally, Werewolf culture is a rough and tumble one of layered fealties. And never forget, a Werewolf is a massive killing machine that lives for the hunt. Hunts are violent things. So again, you might be the protagonist but no hero. These are games of <b><i>personal horror</i></b> after all and there's a good reason why the Kuruth rules are so fearsome. Killing packmates on accident is a thing. And humans are hardly off the menu.<br /> <br /> Given that Beasts can hook their Lairs to one another as a means of combat, it's quite likely that Beasts enjoy a rough and tumble system of almost Darwinian combat to select who's the biggest monster in the Hive. This might change night after night, except that the strength of Beasts waxes and wanes with their Hunger and a new Beast is not that much less powerful than an ancient one. To me this is a good indicator that Beasts gang up on one another -- no lone Beast could be the top dog in the Hive for long as the Lair combat rules makes it easy for groups of Beasts to gang up on individual Beasts. You might object to this on some kind of morality grounds but I think their name says it all--Beast.<br /> <br /> My conclusion is that in a massive cross-over ecosystem the vast majority of Beasts participate in their own internal culture which is one of internecine &quot;gang&quot; warfare as the various &quot;gangs&quot; smash their group Lairs into one another. A small handful of &quot;outsider&quot; Beasts hang with other supernaturals. Those who hang with Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, or Changelings must accept that they have a precarious status in those social groups and might easily find themselves used as pawns in the machinations of the &quot;movers and shakers&quot; and so their status is little better than pets because they must rely on their Kin to protect them from their Kin's Kin. Those hanging out with Demons, Hunters, and Sin-eaters (or Revenants as I call them) might actually enjoy some amount of power over their &quot;Kin&quot; as they bring valuable abilities to the table. Those hanging out with loner splats like Prometheans (or Monsters as I call them), Mummies, or Deviants are the ones most likely to enjoy the companionship of actual equals. YMMV but the rulebook provides the tools that it provides, all else is left for us to hack or ignore. And in no universe are Beasts over-powered (which is the topic here after all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T07:23:56-08:00","id":842550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842527#post842527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could use an ability sorta like a Demon's spoofing ability that let's them either remain under the radar or makes them look like too much trouble to eat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually.. beasts CAN spoof being one of the other splats so long as they have a kinship bond.<br /> <br /> Its described on page 90 of the current backer version as 'passing resemblance' and the whole segment discusses exactly what this thread has been debating concerning how beasts safely enter the cultures of other splats. The gist of it is, they can spend one will power per scene and from that point on, they appear to be that sort of creature to ALL supernatural senses until they end the effect or the scene ends.. it cannot be used multiple times per scene however.<br /> <br /> It automatically fools passive sense abilities, and active 'scans' become a clash of wills. If the beast has a high satiety rating (7+) the deception also includes superficial but convincing illusory elements such as projecting a crude fae mein while imitating a changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T07:34:22-08:00","id":842554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842550#post842550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually.. beasts CAN spoof being one of the other splats so long as they have a kinship bond.<br /> <br /> Its described on page 90 of the current backer version as 'passing resemblance' and the whole segment discusses exactly what this thread has been debating concerning how beasts safely enter the cultures of other splats. The gist of it is, they can spend one will power per scene and from that point on, they appear to be that sort of creature to ALL supernatural senses until they end the effect or the scene ends.. it cannot be used multiple times per scene however.<br /> <br /> It automatically fools passive sense abilities, and active 'scans' become a clash of wills. If the beast has a high satiety rating (7+) the deception also includes superficial but convincing illusory elements such as projecting a crude fae mein while imitating a changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's still a pretty thin defense if you find yourself in front of a bunch of Harpies at Elysium (or really if you end up crossing paths with any elder Vampire). It's main problem is that it simply falls over if someone Lashes Out (or any number of other mental/spiritual clashes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T08:00:17-08:00","id":842566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842209#post842209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More generally, it seems like you are generalizing pretty hard, and if that's how you play that's fine, but not every Vampire wants to Blond Bond the whole world in the default setting. Same goes for the other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't the third drink from someone shattered the other bonds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T08:36:11-08:00","id":842582,"title":"","content":"Jacob, you realize Lashing Out and equivalents are blunt non-physical aggression tools that may constitute social faux pas and transgressions of standard etiquette, and are not just used nilly-willy? And that the All-Night Society relies on that foundation of if not respect then civility to work?<br /> <br /> I find it strange you treat the matter of morality so dismissively when all CofD games are based on a humanist standpoint and the personal horror in Requiem relies heavily on the shaky descent into monstruous detachment in contrast to human sympathies and empathy.<br /> <br /> More disconcertingly, your claims that you understand the games and they support your interpretations ring inconsistent when you seem to have been unaware of some of the most puissant social tools available to Beasts, and indeed ignorant of nuances and details in various lines that are relevant to the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-05-2016, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T11:36:06-08:00","id":842662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842069#post842069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes Beasts even scarier, in my opinion, at mostly at High Satiety, is how they clearly incentivize all these specialists to come together, providing an undeniably amazing safe-place that can help increase mobility in several ways, skew the environments to their advantage, strengthen them, front-run for them, etc. Beasts provide a great platform for everyone else to stand on and shine with, and in doing so provides himself a retinue of exceptional skill.<br /> <br /> There's a reason I tend towards the Lord of the Castle/Master of Monsters angle of Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div> I always thought that angle was awesome. In fact, I've been trying to come up with a multi-splat Brood led by a Beast that works as a mobile detective team, with their equivalent of a Mystery Machine being a Skafoi Wonder that is bigger on the inside like the TARDIS. They may or may not be government-sanctioned. I imagine that, if supernaturals existed IRL, goverments would not ignore the possibility of hiring them as specialized task forces, intelligence gatherers and so on. After all, other nations might be doing the same. Better safe than sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-05-2016, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T11:48:26-08:00","id":842668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842482#post842482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have time to answer the whole post, sorry if I seem to be cherry picking. But i strongly disagree with this, You Must Obey easily being among the worst Dominate-alike out of any splat.<br /> It requires heavy babysitting of those you dominate, only lasts a scene, is limited on the number of orders you can give and orders can be ignored with a breaking point roll..</div> </div> </div> </div>That's okay. I understand what you're saying; I guess I should have qualified &quot;best of&quot; more directly. For me it's simply the ability to no-fuss-no-muss get off a single action and then be able to issue multiple stacked complex commands. Since you get so MANY if you're above the Satiety threshold, I'd also disagree with the babysitting in that anything I need to get done I probably have room to describe getting done. I'm also not certain that complex orders are capped at your Satiety or if that's just the QUEUE of complex orders, but either way, I think the occasions where you need more commands in a single scene but can't stay near the victim (even with, say, your stealth kit) are gonna be few and far between.<br /> <br /> They CAN take Breaking Points to ignore your commands, but that's probably something they'll reserve for actions that are normally Breaking Points, which will stop Dominate 1 and CAN stop Dominate 3, and unlike Dominate they don't do so automatically once they start to bleed for the cause. This is true even if you're using the low Satiety version and that actually is significant because it opens up some uses Dominate CAN'T do, like effective forced conscription - if you can get them into a firefight at all, and they survive, they'll continue following your commands normally. With Dominate, if they get shot you lose control, so even if the command worked they're now as like to bolt or surrender as to keep going.<br /> <br /> Also and somewhat horrifyingly, nothing stops a Beast who isn't really pressed for time from just slamming a victim with Breaking Points over and over until they lose their previous inhibition towards whatever you asked them to do. Any attempt to ignore or countermand your orders triggers a Breaking Point - but doesn't end the power.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Scene-length duration IS a downside, but I personally just don't rate that highly enough to take too much away from the thing you're being enabled to do. A Ventrue gets more duration, but they have about the same raw efficacy, and the Beast still has room for more stuff because that's just one Nightmare. But this is all my perspective, based on the games I play in and the kind of use-cases that come up: any NPC who doesn't a name and a place in the setting already I probably don't NEED for more than a scene, for instance, has been my experience. Security guards, cops, people in hospitals, people whose house I need to be inside, people I need to interrogate, et cetera. Generally once-and-done folk. Making a major NPC my long-term puppet is where Majesty shines, but not quite at Majesty 3 IMHO.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, the Satiety Expenditure version can be used to refill Willpower or provide an Exceptional Success buff that you can make power-relevant by knowing what command you need to give. That's actually something I'm uncomfortable with in terms of power. Actually I'm a lot uncomfortable with it, there is zero sanity check on that usage aside from Rule Zero'ing the absolute fuck out of it. That's literally a potential 1 Willpower/action drip, right? They choose the benefit before rolling so if you know you're starting a fight, have another let you tag them, issue command (careful with your language of course) and now they're in overdrive beyond I think what is reasonable for a single Nightmare. Why?! Now I'm upset.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> On the offchance that anyone's watching, by the way, it would be nice to have official clarification: I am pretty certain that we're all right that Breaking Points are a trade against at least the specific command you've been given, but it doesn't actually SAY they don't still follow the command - it references attempts only, although I expect that's the intention otherwise why mention it at all. Something something natural language, I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","user":"Kingdom of One","date":". 03-05-2016, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T13:21:20-08:00","id":842699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842668#post842668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They CAN take Breaking Points to ignore your commands, but that's probably something they'll reserve for actions that are normally Breaking Points, which will stop Dominate 1 and CAN stop Dominate 3, and unlike Dominate they don't do so automatically once they start to bleed for the cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but unlike Dominate you get the <i>option </i>to resist even if the action wouldn't normally be a breaking point. Which can make all the difference, because IMO reliability is the one most important aspect of a Dominate power, which You Will Obey is lacking more than basically any other. Even if you just order them to silently stand in a corner they might end up resisting, so you can never be 100% sure of your orders being followed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842668#post842668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also and somewhat horrifyingly, nothing stops a Beast who isn't really pressed for time from just slamming a victim with Breaking Points over and over until they lose their previous inhibition towards whatever you asked them to do. Any attempt to ignore or countermand your orders triggers a Breaking Point - but doesn't end the power.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just ends up feeding your target Beats for getting Breaking Points and maybe lowering their Integrity a few points.Nothing about how Integrity works could lead to them losing their previous inhibitions, as Integrity rating has no influence on your behaviour. It's an abstraction with the sole result of providing different dice modifiers on your Breaking Point rolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingdom of One</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842668#post842668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the offchance that anyone's watching, by the way, it would be nice to have official clarification: I am pretty certain that we're all right that Breaking Points are a trade against at least the specific command you've been given, but it doesn't actually SAY they don't still follow the command - it references attempts only, although I expect that's the intention otherwise why mention it at all. Something something natural language, I know.</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation would be that if you don't do what You Must Obey wants you to do you suffer a Breaking Point. You don't do it whether you succeed or fail, the possible effect on your Integrity is the only repercussion.<br /> <br /> One other downside to You Must Obey is that it requires the victim to either look you in the eyes - which is a mistake it will only do once, or never if they are preinformed - or for you to touch them. I think Dominate has a similar drawback, but Mage Dominate for example and probably some others don't.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, I don't think You Must Obey is garbarge or anything like that. Just that it's slightly weaker than the Dominate powers other splats have and most definitely isn't &quot;best of Dominate in a neat one-Nightmare package&quot; (which is the part I mostly disagree with and wanted to comment on).<br /> When I think of the &quot;best parts of Dominate&quot; I think of stuff like long term control and being 100% predictable and reliable if you know your target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 03-05-2016, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T15:55:41-08:00","id":842755,"title":"","content":"A reasonable assessment of the drawbacks on You Must Obey, but you forgot about Conditions. Failing a Breaking Point roll, or even succeeding at one, leaves the character Shaken, Spooked, or Guilty, which contributes to social pliability. A Dramatic Failure, which becomes more likely as integrity drops, leads to Broken or Fugue, at which point resisting further uses of the power is highly unlikely.<br /> <br /> Also, as with all Nightmares it can be set to activate only when the victim next sleeps, so especially with the high Satiety queue effect there's a reasonable amount of leeway to accomplish things without having to be present.<br /> <br /> I agree that it's still not as good as a full 5 dots of Dominate but it's not exactly weak either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T16:09:38-08:00","id":842761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Points 1 and 2 are just silly. Vampires are monsters. They might be protagonists but in no world are they heroes. Morality isn't a thing in CofD games and asking them not to use Blood Bonds is effectively asking them to walk around with one arm tied around their back. Never forget, Vampires are blood-sucking predators that hunt humans for food. </div> </div> </div>Just because someones a vampire doesn't mean they lose their mortality immediately and that all vampires are inhuman evil monsters with no sense of human ethics..... that's why humanity exists as a mechanic.There are vampires who aren't evil assholes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite appearances to the contrary, Humanity 4~6 is the best level to maintain. </div> </div> </div>That's subjective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regarding point 3, I'm not sure I follow. The entire Lashing Out section provides rules for Vampires to assert dominance over one another without resorting to physical violence. </div> </div> </div>Considering the lashing out rules say that doing it against kindred makes it either fight or flight... that makes it an attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Point 4, is also silly. Ghouls go through life Blood Bonded. Many Childer are also likely to. Blood addiction is a core theme to the game afterall. </div> </div> </div>Oh, so because some other people are fine with making people unstable, it's silly to not be fine with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T07:09:48-08:00","id":842967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842164#post842164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could also go for monsters sitcocm. Hell, I almost do it-most of my games tend toward the slice of life angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Full (Moon) House.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T08:03:42-08:00","id":842988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842582#post842582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jacob, you realize Lashing Out and equivalents are blunt non-physical aggression tools that may constitute social faux pas and transgressions of standard etiquette, and are not just used nilly-willy? And that the All-Night Society relies on that foundation of if not respect then civility to work?<br /> <br /> I find it strange you treat the matter of morality so dismissively when all CofD games are based on a humanist standpoint and the personal horror in Requiem relies heavily on the shaky descent into monstruous detachment in contrast to human sympathies and empathy.<br /> <br /> More disconcertingly, your claims that you understand the games and they support your interpretations ring inconsistent when you seem to have been unaware of some of the most puissant social tools available to Beasts, and indeed ignorant of nuances and details in various lines that are relevant to the discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>We agree to disagree. I think you're making things out to be more civilized than they are. Vampires, Werewolves, etc., are aggressive by nature. Their toolsets support this. The inspirational materials support this. The game themes support this.<br /> <br /> You're free to interpret things as you like but you're starting to steer into personal attack and territory. So it's likely best to let things go. You've failed to deliver any actual counterpoint beyond 'you're doing it wrong.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T08:13:30-08:00","id":842991,"title":"","content":"I have done nothing except deliver counterpoints (while criticizing evidenced incomplete or flawed awareness of the source material, yes), but alright. It doesn't seem likely we'll come to an understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-06-2016, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T08:42:44-08:00","id":843000,"title":"","content":"To be fair, with people defending positions they've held for the majority of a year, did anyone actually expect movement?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T09:15:00-08:00","id":843012,"title":"","content":"Hoping against all hope, as they say. Despite my better judgement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T09:51:47-08:00","id":843026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842543#post842543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I apologize if you find this insulting. That is not my intention. We fundamentally disagree on Vampires and likely on CofD games in general.<br /> Points 1 and 2 are just silly. Vampires are monsters. They might be protagonists but in no world are they heroes. Morality isn't a thing in CofD games and asking them not to use Blood Bonds is effectively asking them to walk around with one arm tied around their back. Never forget, Vampires are blood-sucking predators that hunt humans for food.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes human food. The CofD is a large, dark horror world with stuff lurking in its corners that will make even the hardest vampire cry in terror.<br /> Those vampires trying to blood bond unknown horrors willy nilly aren't &quot;Hunters&quot; or &quot;Monsters&quot;, they shortsighted suicidal soon to be victims that won't survive a year.<br /> Blood Bond some dark beast of unknown origin and with unknown abilities? This isn't D&amp;D for Glitterpires, a vampire that makes a habit of this behaviour would be better of taking a sunbath and saving themselves a truckload of trouble.<br /> <br /> In a world that features the kinds of horrors the CofD does not blood bonding everything that crosses your way isn't a matter of &quot;being a hero&quot;, as you so eloquently put it. It's a matter of basic common sense and a functioning survival instinct.<br /> <br /> Or, you know, other vampires egging you on and keeping an eye on you just for the chance to point and laugh when you try your Blood Bond on the wrong target and get eaten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 03-06-2016, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T19:07:37-08:00","id":843239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842543#post842543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize if you find this insulting. That is not my intention. We fundamentally disagree on Vampires and likely on CofD games in general.<br /> Points 1 and 2 are just silly. Vampires are monsters. They might be protagonists but in no world are they heroes. Morality isn't a thing in CofD games and asking them not to use Blood Bonds is effectively asking them to walk around with one arm tied around their back. Never forget, Vampires are blood-sucking predators that hunt humans for food.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all pretty moot considering a third drink from someone shatters the other mid-step bonds. It's not something you can utilize willy nilly. It's not WoD.<br /> <br /> Edit: In fact? An elder would probably only reserve such a bond with the neonate which he has to feed from. Wouldn't you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 03-07-2016, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T06:11:40-08:00","id":843380,"title":"","content":"Blood bonds wither after a year anyway. So every time you bond someone you're making a commitment you supply them with vitae on a regular, if infrequent, basis. For one or two thralls that's not a big deal, but it will quickly add up if you try to bond everyone you meet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T06:30:19-08:00","id":843385,"title":"","content":"In my last vampire game one of the player characters owned a bar and would dose drinks to ensure continued attendance.<br /> <br /> Some vampires may feel blood bonding others is wrong, others will have no problem with it. Just like some Beasts may not want to expend Satiety or slaughter people, and others might be fine with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-07-2016, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T09:19:16-08:00","id":843474,"title":"","content":"I think the most powerful social control that Changelings have access too isn't even a social power normally at all, its only becomes one with the Fairest effect.<br /> <br /> Hidden Reality Contract with the Fairest Effect.<br /> <br /> Take an adorable innocent girl Scout and turn her from a Sweetheart into Bloodthirsty Cannibal. Take a take a dominate Vampire and charge his disposition to servile, or obediant. Take a coward and make her brave. Take a make a Christian an Athetist. Make a Raging Werewolf Tranquil. Make pyscho slasher remorseful. Make a demon honest. Make a loyal Angel rebellious and watch as they fall (while the Angel's personality might return to loyal, it won't change that they've fallen). Make some who hates your guts be passionately in love with you.<br /> <br /> And that's not even the powers main purpose, it a side benifit.<br /> <br /> The Changeling can too so many sublte, but powerful things with Hidden Reality, more so with both the Wizened and Fairest Effects.<br /> <br /> I don't think beasts or vampires have anything, not even dominate that beats it.<br /> <br /> Oh look the door too your house is unlocked, could have sworn you locked it before you lets? Oh well. You thought your wife hated me, oh it looks like she positively jubiliant to see me. She made me her famous roast beef, that you didn't realize you had in your freezer. Is that your Porche, the one never had in the garage and the keys for it on your coffee table? Excuse while I go joy riding in your Poreche with your wife. Oh I found your spare wallet in the glove buck, and its filled with cash? You don't remember having a spare wallet. Well I guess you won't mind me using these credit cards you never applied for or using the condom you have in it then.<br /> <br /> See how powerful Hidden Reality with all the Seeming perks can be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T09:24:24-08:00","id":843476,"title":"","content":"For combat Phantom Glory + Elemental Effect, none solid element, you immune physical damage, your body becomes a 2 damage weapon, and you can move through solid objects. Tough to beat that, especially when the Changeling has a combat Kith.<br /> <br /> A Soldier Kith Changeling can switch around his fight style merits daily, so if she starts off with 10 fighting style merits then the Soldier can basically be the master of any two given fighting styles at a time and more as more merits are aquired.<br /> <br /> Again I don't know of any other splat that can do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 03-07-2016, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T09:50:37-08:00","id":843494,"title":"","content":"I think multisplat cooperation is the Beasts specialization, aka what it does better then anyone else. It can access any of the other splats special locations, hedge, shadow, underworld, Astral, possibly weirder things like emanation realms, maybe even the Inferno, and the world were the Strix come from (which is terrifying when you think of the havok a beast can cause unleasing monsters from other worlds).<br /> <br /> The Beast can pretend to be other splats.<br /> <br /> The Beast can feed on other splats hunts and enhance those splats.<br /> <br /> And it can gain new nightmares based on other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T16:18:28-08:00","id":843662,"title":"","content":"Kinship Nightmares are quite possibly the biggest reason for other splats to be wary of trying to tame Beasts. Whatever your greatest weakness is, spend too long with a Beast and they'll likely learn a Nightmare that exploits it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T19:29:25-08:00","id":843748,"title":"","content":"And for the fun not even technically malicious intent in developing a kinship nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T21:05:37-08:00","id":843792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=843662#post843662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinship Nightmares are quite possibly the biggest reason for other splats to be wary of trying to tame Beasts. Whatever your greatest weakness is, spend too long with a Beast and they'll likely learn a Nightmare that exploits it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remain unconvinced. This sounds like a great way to end up in someone's cross hairs. At any rate this convo has gotten relatively off topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T21:25:45-08:00","id":843807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=843792#post843792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like a great way to end up in someone's cross hairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a great reason not to spend a lot of time around the fledgeling mirror-monster whose common developmental paths include &quot;grow past the point where feeding through you is less trouble than feeding on you,&quot; but yes, I'm sure there exist characters who think the concept of Children growing up to be dangerous to them personally justifies murdering any strange supernatural creature that tries to associate with them in cold blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T05:02:40-08:00","id":843899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=843662#post843662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinship Nightmares are quite possibly the biggest reason for other splats to be wary of trying to tame Beasts. Whatever your greatest weakness is, spend too long with a Beast and they'll likely learn a Nightmare that exploits it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Huh. I never quite looked at it that way before. I always thought of Kinship Nightmares as tapping into the nightmares that the splat represents to humans, not what nightmares they have. I guess the anti-hunter comparison runs deeper than I thought.<br /> <br /> EDIT - Or maybe its more that each splat fears what they can do? That's too deep for this early in the morning. Each splat has a balance of human-like and monster-like, and falling to monster-like could be a weakness, I suppose...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-08-2016, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T08:30:38-08:00","id":843977,"title":"","content":"Every splat can, given enough EXP, accomplish any goal. The question is efficiency.<br /> <br /> * Investigation<br /> This is the ability to identify and gain a clearer picture of issues or a plot relevant situation. This can be achieved through the investigation mini game in CoD or by passing it entirely.<br /> <br /> Mortals can bypass the mini game with the Omen Sensitivity merit. They are the baseline for playing the minigame, so Supernaturals will need bonuses beyond what a mortal gets or the ability to get those bonuses more efficiently.<br /> <br /> Vampires can bypass the mini game with Cruac 1 or Auspex 1 (&quot;Who can give me what I want?&quot;). Animalism grants a new information source. Some Vampires can more easily gain contacts. Acute Senses is a one dot merit that let's you add your BP to most investigation rolls. Your innate kindred senses let you add it again in some situations as well as determine whether or not a target is supernatural. <br /> <br /> Werewolves have an additional information source through spirits. Wolf senses can add to investigation rolls. They have no particular way to confirm their targets beyond mundane rolls, though they could default to social maneuvering at that point.<br /> <br /> Changelings have Kiths that can bypass the minigame (antiquitarian, Telluric). They can also boost their dice pools through the roof. Another Kith can read minds to confirm the target. Riddle kith can be used to get all of these kiths.<br /> <br /> Beast gets epic Direction Sense, which can send the Beasts senses back in time. This can often, but not always bypass the minigame. They have no particular advantages with the minigame, and no need to confirm the target.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: Vampires are great at investigating other Vampires and anyone if they pick the right disciplines. Werewolves are better off skipping right to the Hunt. Changelings need riddle kith or a motley of Changelings with the correct combination, but they can bypass the minigame very easily. Beasts can bypass the minigame in most instances using epic direction sense.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, anyone can &quot;win&quot; the investigation minigame with reliable exceptional successes using professional training. Mortal merits grant more effective clues.<br /> <br /> Pretty equal over all. Werewolves slightly behind.<br /> <br /> ** Tracking<br /> Anyone can play the Tracking Minigame to find people.<br /> <br /> Vampires get their BP added once or twice to tracking rolls. Cruac 1 can bypass the minigame sometimes.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are built around the minigame. They get innate bonuses to tracking and impossible spoor.<br /> <br /> Changelings can muscle through anything that is based on a dieroll. Some contracts (particularly the mirror ones) can bypass the minigame. Changelings can also teleport, which means if a Changeling ever knows someone's location they can get there.<br /> <br /> Beasts can bypass the minigame with Epic Direction sense. Look in the past to see who murdered someone and congrats, since you have seen them you always know what direction they are in.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: Werewolves are by default best at the minigame. Vampires at higher BP can match or exceed werewolves so long as the experience is spent and blood is involved. Changelings are the best if they pay all the experience for what they need or make some unsavory goblin vows. Changelings are also the best at bypassing the minigame if they dump the experience into it. Beasts are the most efficiently able to bypass the minigame entirely.<br /> <br /> ** Research<br /> You are probably playing a variety of the investigation minigame. This is about collecting information on a subject.<br /> <br /> Vampires can find out a lot of information from individuals with their powers. Mind reading, mind control, etc. Social Engineering is an amazing Invictus merit for this purpose in many situations. Where the Bodies Are Buried and Cacaphony Savvy are great against other beings connected to vampires. Otherwise, they don't have much.<br /> <br /> Werewolves can find out a lot about target's traits and weaknesses I'd they purchase the proper gifts. This usually requires the werewolf be face to face.<br /> <br /> Changelings with the correct kith (omen sensitivity) can easily research things in one room if they know the correct questions. They can also strong-arm anything with dice. They can get mind reading through another kith.<br /> <br /> Beasts get Mimir's Wisdom which can give them advanced library to cover exactly what they need. Also has some mold information gathering powers when you can see your target.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: Beast wins against distant topics you cant see. Vampires (specifically invictus) are best at getting general blackmail or information about ither vampires. Everything becomes evenish if you can see your target face to face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 03-08-2016, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T09:25:41-08:00","id":844004,"title":"","content":"*** Social Maneuvering<br /> Everyone is more or less even at tasks that only require a single roll. Emphasis will be placed on situations requiring social maneuvering, long term control, and/or bypassing the minigame.<br /> <br /> Everyone has access to Sympathetic, Fast-Talking, and Pusher which allows someone to hypothetically open 4 doors on a single roll--5 on an exceptional.<br /> <br /> Vampires have a lot here. By default they have blood bonds (a dice bonus and automatic better impressions). They have a lot of powers that bypass social maneivering entirely (i.e. Dominate and Majesty). They don't actually interact with the system itself much.<br /> <br /> Werewolves can improve the number of doors required to achieve a goal on their pack mates through a gift. They can also improve impressions for immediately executable goals. They have a smattering of dice Stimson and impressions improving powers if someone cares to invest. They don't have many ways to bypass the system.<br /> <br /> Changelings can bum rush doors efficiently with the correct Kith (Flowering, Deerheart, many others). Mask of Superiority's Fairest bonus can open up to three doors. Oneiromancy, however, bares particular mention. Convince the dreamer let's you convince people of things slowly over time from a million miles away, and it is a default power. That is on top of stock ppwers to alter memories. Their effects to bypass the maneuvering system are otherwise limited, with a lot of effects to keep someone from acting. Of particular note for Changelings is that one four dot gift that let's them, with the fairest bonus, edit people's personalities from any distance with no resistance roll. It's... yeah. I wouldn't be surprised if it didn't make the to the end in its current form.<br /> <br /> Beasts get more effective Hard Leverage through Nightmares by default. You Must Obey is bypass of questionable power. They can pump up their dice pool through the roof, but that only helps so much. Alien Allure is at first brush the winner (particularly the constant good impression), but keep in mind that Atavisms use is obvious to supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Conclusions: By default, with no investment, Changelings win just because of Oneiromancy. Changelings remain king of tearing down doors at all EXP levels. Hidden Reality also bears special mention. Vampires, with the correct social powers, are hands down the best at bypassing the system in the widest range of situations. Werewolves can achieve immediate goals by spamming rolls, but lag behind on anything else. Beasts are amazing at bullying people and giving them a very bad day, but less so in any other area.<br /> <br /> *** Social Merits<br /> <br /> Vampires can be pretty good at this. Most of their ability centers around merits pulling double or triple duty. Carthians and Invictus are both good at different subsets of it. Long term, *some* vampire concepts are absolutely amazing at this.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have Residential Area. This means on their home turf they are amazing. Otherwise... meh.<br /> <br /> Changelings get Mask of Superiority, which is Status/Allies [Everything] 3. ... that's really all you need. Like seriously. Okay, not enough? Goblin Vow.<br /> <br /> Beasts don't really have anything in this area. One could argue the opportunity to buy merits representing ties to other supernatural groups but that is very campaign specific.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: Changelings win, hands down. Some vampire concepts eventually win more by having their merits pull double or triple duty. Werewolves and Beasts are pretty mediocre.<br /> <br /> *** Chases<br /> Irrelevant. Parkour 5 and the merit that makes you start with Edge is, hands down, the best bang for your buck. Okay, that's not *entirely* true.<br /> <br /> Vampires can bypass getting chased with Obfuscate and/or Protean. Celerity gives a vampire lots of speed but, far more importantly, it let's them go first. It is often the case that the person going first will win.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are probably king of footchases, or at least very much up there. The wolf form gives you a great default dice pool and higher than normal speed. The wolf monster for let's you cheat the action order, which as stated above is very important.<br /> <br /> Changelings are probably the best at getting away so long as they have a relevant contract and are able to fulfill the catch. Nevertread, Thorns and Brambles, Hedgewall, etc etc etc. They can also teleport in a couple of different ways.<br /> <br /> Beasts have nothing particularly interesting regarding chases. A couple of speed bonuses and extra ways to move or teleport. They want to deny the chase entirely by drawing the person into their Lair or using a Nightmare.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: Out of the gate, Werewolves are the best. Vampires can match or exceed them with enough EXP. Changelings have a ton of tricks to help them get away, but not as many for catching people. Beasts need to shove people into their Lair or create tons of penalties if they want to &quot;chase.&quot; Otherwise they are just a bit better than mortals.<br /> <br /> *** Stealth<br /> <br /> Vampire: Obfuscate 3 and Celerity 1+.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: Have a lot of powers that grant bonuses for stealth and penalties to notice them. They can also their stealth rolls with others. The Gauntlet, at higher amounts of exp, can be am effective infiltration tool.<br /> <br /> Changelings win hands down if we include disguise in this category. In terms of mundane stealth Changeling can strong-arm their pool and supply significant penalties to notice them. Night's Subtle Distractions let's them perform stealth actions reflexively, which is *huge*. Although expensive, Phantom Glory can render them truly invisible to most opponents.<br /> <br /> Beasts get an Atavism to help with this considerably, though true invisibility requires saity. There is also a nightmare that can make someone ignore one subject, which is more situational but very effective when you can pull it off.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: A vampire that invests in stealth wins, hands down. Beasts are a close second by virtue of having a power that requires a clash to bypass. Changelings win at disguise and they win the strong arm mundane pools game. Werewolves bring up the rear, but it's important to note they are still good at stealth--other slats are just better.<br /> <br /> *** Crafting<br /> <br /> Vampires have nothing special here.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have fetishes and some dice pool bonuses.<br /> <br /> Changelings win at this using the correct kiths, period. They get significant bonuses. They can complete large scale works as instant and automatically successful actions. They get magic items with a variety of effects they can build.<br /> <br /> Beasts get nothing special here.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: Changelings win, period.werewolves are in second place because they have fetishes and dice bonuses. Vampires and Beasts just don't touch on crafting.<br /> <br /> *** Combat<br /> ...is complicated and will need to be it's own post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T10:02:52-08:00","id":844024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=843899#post843899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought of Kinship Nightmares as tapping into the nightmares that the splat represents to humans, not what nightmares they have.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> EDIT - Or maybe its more that each splat fears what they can do? That's too deep for this early in the morning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinship Nightmares distill the fears associated with a given family member regardless of which direction they're applied - the nonspecific ones for werewolves, mages, Prometheans, changelings and mummies all directly key off of a problem that those splats personally experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T12:29:02-08:00","id":844098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844004#post844004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*** Combat<br /> ...is complicated and will need to be it's own post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Just go with your usual &quot;Changeling with the right combination of Kiths, goblin fruit, contracts and magic dream items win. Period.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T13:45:28-08:00","id":844128,"title":"","content":"Eh. Any starting Kith, Riddle-Kith, Phantom Glory [+Elemental], and Mask of Supremacy 3 gets you basically everything you could need for what I posted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T14:29:08-08:00","id":844150,"title":"","content":"Changelings are specialists. If you're going to compare splats, do it with universal template mechanics only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T14:35:54-08:00","id":844155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=843977#post843977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Investigation<br /> This is the ability to identify and gain a clearer picture of issues or a plot relevant situation. This can be achieved through the investigation mini game in CoD or by passing it entirely.<br /> ....<br /> Werewolves have an additional information source through spirits. Wolf senses can add to investigation rolls. They have no particular way to confirm their targets beyond mundane rolls, though they could default to social maneuvering at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's Echo Dream, which tells you what happened in the past in the location you're in, which would be pretty useful for finding out who murdered someone there. Also Eyes of the Dead, which would show you the last moments of the victim's life as well as the name of everyone they saw during it, providing the victim knew their name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T15:03:18-08:00","id":844166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=842201#post842201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We don't actually have enough rules to really know what this means. (IIRC, Heroes might be some kind of necessary factor.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, what part of the Incarnate rules do you feel is insufficient to explain their capabilities? (That's not meant as snark, by the way: since I wrote it originally, I'm keen to know.)<br /> <br /> (Although, yes, Heroes are a necessary factor for a Beast to become an Incarnate.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T15:30:53-08:00","id":844177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844166#post844166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiosity, what part of the Incarnate rules do you feel is insufficient to explain their capabilities? (That's not meant as snark, by the way: since I wrote it originally, I'm keen to know.)<br /> <br /> (Although, yes, Heroes are a necessary factor for a Beast to become an Incarnate.)</div> </div> </div> </div> If I remember correctly, a Beast needs Lair 8+, and then they have to completely curb-stomp a Hero. Not even one point of lethal damage can be taken and no surprise can make the Beast falter. I don't remember if the Hero has to die, but he/she must be <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HumiliationConga\" target=\"_blank\"><b>so humiliated and devastated</b></a> that they give up on being a Hero, showing the Beast to be the undisputed master of their own story, not a trophy in the Hero's story. I think it's more fun to spare the Hero so he/she can live knowing they were wrong from the very beginning. Bonus points if the battle involves the Beast showing how the Hero's Legend will never compare to the Beast's Legend + Hunger.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T17:35:59-08:00","id":844229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844128#post844128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. Any starting Kith, Riddle-Kith, Phantom Glory [+Elemental], and Mask of Supremacy 3 gets you basically everything you could need for what I posted.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844150#post844150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings are specialists. If you're going to compare splats, do it with universal template mechanics only.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I just looked through your analysis, and well, you gave changelings their choice of Kith into the consideration without giving similar treatment to the other splats for ALL of your examination. No Clan, no Auspice, ect.<br /> <br /> This results in what is arguably skewed results and is a very clear author bias. You may wish to go back and edit your post to atleast include &quot;neutral kith&quot; examination.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T18:01:01-08:00","id":844243,"title":"","content":"Or at least talk about about how Clan/Auspice and the like factor into the equation. You may have even taken them into consideration, but your post doesn't really indicate such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T19:57:42-08:00","id":844297,"title":"","content":"Eh, Elodoth can also get any social merit they wish at 5 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 03-08-2016, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T20:07:23-08:00","id":844301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844166#post844166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Although, yes, Heroes are a necessary factor for a Beast to become an Incarnate.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Were, I thought, unless we've reverted the process to purely run on the Subvert The Hero model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T20:42:55-08:00","id":844325,"title":"","content":"Last draft I checked becoming a city's Apex or somehow revealing your legend to the world at large are also options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T21:04:42-08:00","id":844333,"title":"","content":"Why eat a hero when you can eat your fellow beasts? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T02:56:58-08:00","id":844413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844301#post844301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were, I thought, unless we've reverted the process to purely run on the Subvert The Hero model.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's quite possible, true. Admittedly, since I didn't use any of the endgame types in the <b>Beast</b> game I ran at GenCon last year, I didn't revisit that section during prep. So my information might be slightly outdated, then. Apologies for misinformation. I'll have to go back and double-check it later this evening when I get home from work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T06:12:07-08:00","id":844467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=843977#post843977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every splat can, given enough EXP, accomplish any goal. The question is efficiency.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ummm.... your analysis is missing a lot of things. Like, in Investigation when talking about werewolves? Insight and Knowledge Gifts? Death Gifts can let you eat bones and read what happen? Werewolves have a ton of investigative methods you don't even touch. For Tracking, you just touch on Kindred Senses for vampires, don't bother with the ways you can use Auspex or various rituals to track someone, let alone potentially employing blood sympathy with Coils as well. Again with Research - don't have much? Putting aside that I was specifically talking about doing research on supernaturals / ephemeral entities and Libraries (everything else tends to fall under Investigation rules), you completely ignore the vast libraries and divination powers that most supernatural splats have. <br /> <br /> I could go on, but I'm just going to sum things up here: You are missing too much to have this to have any meaning. People might not like the conclusions I've drawn, and some may argue that I'm biased, but I did my best to ensure that I looked at every possible ability of every splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T06:13:32-08:00","id":844468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844413#post844413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, that's quite possible, true. Admittedly, since I didn't use any of the endgame types in the <b>Beast</b> game I ran at GenCon last year, I didn't revisit that section during prep. So my information might be slightly outdated, then. Apologies for misinformation. I'll have to go back and double-check it later this evening when I get home from work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't looked at the Incarnation rules lately either, but I do know that they were revised as well. Supposedly a lot less &quot;take out the Heroes!&quot; than the original one was. Admittedly, the original one was pretty bad - it was all about perfectly murdering someone, and actually proving that the Beast was actually the monster the Hero thought they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-09-2016, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T06:42:24-08:00","id":844477,"title":"","content":"You still need a Lair trait of at least 8, then you need to solidify your Legend. Either by subverting the Hero, which involves controlling a battle with the Hero and having it entirely on the Beast's terms without getting any Lethal damage or Anathema, at which point they reform their Horror and their humanity is eliminated and they no longer feel anything for their human or supernatural family. Or she can take control of the Hive, which involves showing superiority over other Beasts and 'the most powerful' supernatural in the area, Beast or not, that has contact with humanity. Lastly, she can just create a Legend through spreading a legend of her acts, similar to how a Legend Slasher becomes a Legend, except she must keep Heroes or other Beasts from subverting the Legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-09-2016, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T10:09:22-08:00","id":844578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844468#post844468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't looked at the Incarnation rules lately either, but I do know that they were revised as well. Supposedly a lot less &quot;take out the Heroes!&quot; than the original one was. Admittedly, the original one was pretty bad - it was all about perfectly murdering someone, and actually proving that the Beast was actually the monster the Hero thought they were.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually I've been thinking about the whole &quot;pretty bad&quot; angle lately and am starting to wish that Heroes weren't mortals (or mortal+) but were some kind of nightmare-claimed. If Horrors are the nightmares of humans then heroes work rather nicely as the nightmares of Beasts. Among other things this shifts the fulcrum point from subverting the hero to subverting the monomyth and releasing both Beast and mortal from its grip. But all these boats have kinda sailed since the manuscript is getting indexed and full release is imminent...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T11:41:14-08:00","id":844637,"title":"","content":"If you (general you, to clarify) thought the Incarnate Inheritance would ever make the Beast less of a monster, I can safely say you missed the point. From the material available from the kickstarter, it was never about that. It was about not being <i>someone else's monster</i>. It was about breaking the mold of the monomyth and establishing your own legend, by proving to the world that the story of the Hero is meaningless before your power. To become your own monster, on no one else's terms. A Begotten who utterly defeats a Hero is not the monster the latter thought they were. They are the monster who has shown they are more important than the Hero. That's why Incarnates can shut them down and deny their power.<br /> <br /> I think the addition of alternate ways to achieve it and the possibility to destabilize the Myth was a definite improvement though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-09-2016, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T12:03:24-08:00","id":844654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844637#post844637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you (general you, to clarify) thought the Incarnate Inheritance would ever make the Beast less of a monster, I can safely say you missed the point. From the material available from the kickstarter, it was never about that. It was about not being <i>someone else's monster</i>. It was breaking the mold of the monomyth to establish your own legend by proving to the world that the story of the Hero is meaningless before your power. To truly become your own monster, on no one else's terms. That's why Incarnates can also shut down Heroes.<br /> <br /> I think the addition of other ways to achieve it and the possibility to destabilize the Myth were definite improvements though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though a probable Watsonian explanation for the Incarnate Inheritance is that it's a non-adoptive failsafe for the problem the Children hypothesize has derailed Heroes and Menkhaf suggests has overstimulated the Begotten appetite, given the process effectively brings the character into stronger alignment with the Dream and lessens a lot of the incentives against running your upkeep primarily on nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T12:27:20-08:00","id":844667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844578#post844578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I've been thinking about the whole &quot;pretty bad&quot; angle lately and am starting to wish that Heroes weren't mortals (or mortal+) but were some kind of nightmare-claimed. If Horrors are the nightmares of humans then heroes work rather nicely as the nightmares of Beasts. Among other things this shifts the fulcrum point from subverting the hero to subverting the monomyth and releasing both Beast and mortal from its grip. But all these boats have kinda sailed since the manuscript is getting indexed and full release is imminent...</div> </div> </div> </div> There are a lot of problematic elements in Beast. Heroes and the execution among them. But, if you just made the heroes into Nightmare claimed, you'd be stepping too closely to just having a Beast antagonist, since that's a pretty close description of the Beasts themselves. I think that's too much overlap, personally. Heroes, imho, are basicall a specialized hunter Endowment. These are a completely separate niche. I mean, I understand your point, but there's issues both ways.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844637#post844637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you (general you, to clarify) thought the Incarnate Inheritance would ever make the Beast less of a monster, I can safely say you missed the point.<br /> <br /> From the material available from the kickstarter, it was never about that. It was about not being <i>someone else's monster</i>. It was about breaking the mold of the monomyth and establishing your own legend, by proving to the world that the story of the Hero is meaningless before your power. To become your own monster, on no one else's terms. A Begotten who utterly defeats a Hero is not the monster the latter thought they were. They are the monster who has shown they are more important than the Hero. That's why Incarnates can shut them down and deny their power.<br /> <br /> I think the addition of alternate ways to achieve it and the possibility to destabilize the Myth was a definite improvement though.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think anyone is saying anything about being less of a monster. The problem I had with the old way is that it didn't subvert the old Hero-monster monomyth. It <i>upheld </i>it. You basically played the part of the evil monster that just happened to beat the hero in the story instead of the hero winning. You tormented or killed someone for the sake of power. That's the only difference, and I don't think of that as a subversion. There's no undermining or questioning of the established order here. Unless you count the monster winning, but hey, guess what. The monsters have been winning pretty much up to this point anyways - otherwise, they wouldn't be alive to try for Inheritance.<br /> <br /> And, yeah, if the message was about &quot;not being someone's monster&quot; then the message failed. You were someone's monster. You just won the fight because you were a bigger badass than the Hero was. It just reinforced the whole &quot;Good Versus Evil&quot; trope. The Beast <i>needed</i> the Hero and the fight and the violence and the glory from the struggle as much as the Hero did.<br /> <br /> Now, there was a story about rejecting being someone else's monster in that first pre-revision pdf. It was the short about Beast getting on a plane, and being confronted by a Hero, demanding to know why she was leaving. And the woman just gave an offhand comment about the fight not being worth it, and left everything behind. Now THAT was a good rejection of the monster-hero cycle. Not the whole &quot;I must defeat the Chosen One so I can become All Powerful!&quot; trope of the old Inheritance.<br /> <br /> EDIT - sure, that's all old news. That's why there was such a huge uproar over the matter, and why things were changed. This all clearly wasn't the intent that the writers wanted, but failed to properly portray to the readers. Things changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-09-2016, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T12:41:52-08:00","id":844682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844654#post844654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though a probable Watsonian explanation for the Incarnate Inheritance is that it's a non-adoptive failsafe for the problem the Children hypothesize has derailed Heroes and Menkhaf suggests has overstimulated the Begotten appetite, given the process effectively brings the character into stronger alignment with the Dream and lessens a lot of the incentives against running your upkeep primarily on nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting consideration, as the narrative certainly seems to have gone awry somewhere, with humanity and the Begotten both the worse for it. That the Incarnate Inheritance changes one's relations to the ecology of the Dream in a way that gives their predations more breathing room seems to suggest it exists for a reason beyond allowing Beasts to opt out of a cycle that's become twisted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844667#post844667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone is saying anything about being less of a monster. The problem I had with the old way is that it didn't subvert the old Hero-monster monomyth. It <i>upheld </i>it. You basically played the part of the evil monster that just happened to beat the hero in the story instead of the hero winning. You tormented or killed someone for the sake of power. That's the only difference, and I don't think of that as a subversion. There's no undermining or questioning of the established order here. Unless you count the monster winning, but hey, guess what. The monsters have been winning pretty much up to this point anyways - otherwise, they wouldn't be alive to try for Inheritance.<br /> <br /> The old Inhertiance felt a lot like becoming a psychopathic killer for power and pleasure. Unlike Changeling, where something similar happens for the creation of the True Fae, the Inheritance is generally accepted as a good thing. There are very few things in the CofD that I would classify as &quot;evil.&quot; The Maeljin/Infernal. The Abyss. The Judges of Death and Apep. And that old Inheritance was the fourth. The old Inheritance, to me, wasn't become an advanced monster. It was becoming a force of evil. I don't even classify the strix or Gentry as definitively evil, and pre-revised Beasts made that cut.<br /> <br /> So, its not an issue of being &quot;more or less of a monster.&quot; Being a monster in the CofD has more to do with having abilities and nature beyond the ken of mere mortals than your moral balance. I have no qualms with the former being portrayed as desirable. I have less issues with needing to feed to survive. The problem is with the latter - promotion of destructive actions being desirable. Its a crappy message.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say I share the same views, as I find it did (and does) adequately represent a manner of subversion of the monomyth as a ritual gateway to changing the nature of the Begotten. It wasn't a positive message (and still isn't, really), but that's a consequence of the damaged circumstances and a more or less inevitable conclusion towards the legendary monstruosity required to crush the other facet of the story.<br /> <br /> It was... more problematic under the pre-revision paradigms of Heroes. Not that I think the overall nature of the Inheritance has changed, but the path of Subverting The Hero has very different meaning in the way things currently stand. And there's no doubt that it is the cruelest of the known means to become an Incarnate.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Bottom line is, yeah, the altered context from the original draft changed a lot of things. That great short story is still in the book, in the <i>Subversion </i>section of chapter two, and I agree it does depict a good rejection of the cycle. But it's there in the context of subversion as a general theme of Beast, rather than as a conclusion* to their role in the status quo.<br /> <br /> *None of Inheritances are &quot;good&quot; conclusions by ordinary standards. I think that's kind of the point. It's incredibly important to the themes of the game that Beasts <i>can be more than monsters</i>, and the story where the woman just left the Hero and their struggle behind is a fine example of it. But to undergo the Incarnate Inheritance is to subvert the monomyth <i>as</i> a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-09-2016, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T13:11:29-08:00","id":844689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844682#post844682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an interesting consideration, as the narrative certainly seems to have gone awry somewhere, with humanity and the Begotten both the worse for it. That the Incarnate Inheritance changes one's relations to the ecology of the Dream in a way that gives their predations more breathing room seems to suggest it exists for a reason beyond allowing Beasts to opt out of a cycle that's become twisted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite so \u2014 the speculation of a further step in Shen-lung's writeup certainly meshes the goal-driven nature of many other godlike entities in the setting with the general larvality of the Children, and if the notion of the Devouring brings anything to the table conceptually it's that the necessity of clearing space for development is nothing new to most Beasts.<br /> <br /> The &quot;species&quot; has to go <i>somewhere</i> in the current environment, and the vast womb of Horrors is necessarily picky about who gets to be reborn into the stuff of eternal legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T15:04:37-08:00","id":844753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844682#post844682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*None of Inheritances are &quot;good&quot; conclusions by ordinary standards. I think that's kind of the point.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a difference between being uncomfortable with being a rather sadistic psychopathic figure, and wanting &quot;good&quot; Inheritances. Its a fallacy to assume otherwise. Being more monstrous and being &quot;evil&quot; are two separate things in the CofD. The mere fact that you are bringing up &quot;good&quot; is rather confusing and leads me to believe you are assuming something here. Monsters, at least the PC kind, in the CofD thrive in grey areas. For many people, Beast Inheritance crossed the line from grey to black. And that's a problem, because it cuts out interesting stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-09-2016, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T15:29:54-08:00","id":844762,"title":"","content":"Only tangentially related, English is a remarkably stupid language sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T15:37:17-08:00","id":844768,"title":"","content":"That's not what I meant to say. I already acknowledged that subverting the Hero is a cruel path towards the Inheritance, and it is made more so by the very fact there are alternatives. I wasn't implying anything I didn't explicitely state there, just making an aside. I meant to elaborate (as I have now haphazardly done via edit, details in the text to follow instead) that none of the Inheritances are what I would constitute as an ordinarily happy ending. A Beast who wants to be free of the hold of the mythic cycle as themselves has only the option of overtaking it as a monster beyond monsters.<br /> <br /> It's incredibly important to the theme of subversion that Beasts can be more than monsters. They're people, and they don't <i>need</i> to deal with or relate to everything as a hungering horror. The story you mentioned is a great example of that. The Beast eschews playing the role. She refuses to go with the narrative and prove the Hero right, even if this likely won't be her last foe. But she can't rise above the pursuit of Heroes and the monomyth's grip the way an Incarnate can.<br /> <br /> That's why the Incarnate is tragic. For some, it may be everything they ever wanted but didn't know they did until achieving it. For others, it might be a painful and unthinkable decision, because to become an Incarnate is to forgo your Life for a Myth that fully defines you - as a Beast - from then on. The story is bent under your knee and Heros are just footnotes, but it took making yourself a true monster embodied. And one way or another, that way was going to be <i>dark</i>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It may have been <i>too</i> dark or unapologetically monstrous to stand as a meaningful story element representing a notion that ought to have been at least somewhat positive in Beast The Primordial. I won't deny that. It's understandable that it crossed a line for people back in the first version.<br /> <br /> I guess what I was trying to say through all this rambling was, despite that, I was alright with it from a writing standpoint even then because it felt like it <i>wanted</i> to be a very grim and questionable possibility for Beasts in line with a bleak train of thought.<br /> <br /> P.S.: I hate English sometimes. Arc is right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-09-2016, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T16:36:09-08:00","id":844797,"title":"","content":"Even in the original draft there's nothing explicitly stating you have to kill the Hero. Defeat them in combat without suffering lethal damage or an Anathema does probably mean killing in the majority of cases, but the wording at least allows the possibility of a knockout blow.<br /> <br /> Somewhat strangely, the text on becoming an Incarnate mentions that you no longer feel anything for your human or supernatural family, but one of the two example Incarnates still has such close ties to his werewolf allies that they're probably the best bet at destabilizing his Legend, and his human parents might be another weak link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T18:15:29-08:00","id":844836,"title":"","content":"Food for thought. Beasts seem to be the only splat without a &quot;human&quot; end-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T18:26:22-08:00","id":844846,"title":"","content":"@mcn I can grok what you're saying about a Beast antagonist. IMO, there's a bit too much overlap with Hunters yet for my liking (plus the rather arbitrary Integrity 4 or less issue). I feel like I remember a time when Heroes being people with stillborn Horrors for souls was under consideration as an explanation for why Heroes exist but, maybe I'm projecting one of the possible directions I might have taken the text.<br /> <br /> I do wish that there was some other massive antagonist than Heroes. As far as antagonists go Heroes are bit one note for my tastes. But things are as they are. No point really in complaining when the finished product has all but dropped in our laps. I'll just hack at it until I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T18:39:22-08:00","id":844852,"title":"","content":"Second draft Heroes are a good deal more nuanced and interesting. Integrity 4 isn't a requirement, Beasts just tend to run into low integrity Heroes because those are the people who are unstable enough to feel like hunting nightmare monsters will fix whatever is wrong with their life. Higher integrity Heroes absolutely exist they're just more likely to shrug off weird dreams and continue their normal lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T18:47:07-08:00","id":844854,"title":"","content":"Actually, Heroes can be <i>any </i>Integrity level now- it's just the ones completely obsessed with hunting Beasts are of low Integrity. A high-Integrity Hero may be <i>predisposed</i> to think of a Beast as a threat, but when they seek out the monster they can gain wisdom from it- IE. &quot;Hold up, that's not me I don't think. Let me call some people I know so we can sort this out.&quot; The second version of the previews mention that it's not just Beasts who cause ripples in the Primordial Dream, it's anything that causes fear on a wide scale, but that Heroes who aren't obsessed with hunting Beasts can be persuaded to tackle the real problems instead of just going &quot;You're a Beast, I'm a Hero, I know how this goes- DIE!&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, when the problem <i>is </i>a Beast, I imagine even these not-obsessed Heroes would want to deal with it- that's just part of being a Hero -but they wouldn't necessarily jump straight to killing.<br /> <br /> I imagine that back in the day, probably before the Sundering when there weren't hard and fast barriers between the different worlds, Beasts could feed exclusively by inflicting nightmares (like they do involuntarily when Ravenous or Starving) if they so desired because just about everyone could feel the Primordial Dream. Heroes were the special people especially sensitive to it inclined to look into the dark and find out what was there, helping people conquer their fears. If the Beast got greedy, dangerous, or just too close, the Beast became a problem and the Hero took care of it. Basically, the confrontation with the Beast becomes a vehicle for finding wisdom. In monomyth terms, Trials leads to an encounter with the Goddess. The Hero gets their wisdom, doesn't necessarily need to kill the Beast, goes home. I think it's important to remember that there was little difference between a standard neolithic mother goddess and 'The Dark Mother'. Puts the whole thing into a bit of perspective.<br /> <br /> I wondered at the original purpose of Family Resemblance and other powers that let Beasts get to know and imitate other supernatural beings, and I think it has something to do about Beasts as the keepers of wisdom while Heroes were the seekers. Hero approaches Beast, ready to confront them over the disruption in the Dream, and the Beast isn't the problem- but they might know what it is through the grape vine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T19:09:36-08:00","id":844862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The second version of the previews mention that it's not just Beasts who cause ripples in the Primordial Dream, it's anything that causes fear on a wide scale. </div> </div> </div>.... so politicians and mainstream media networks can be the targets of Heroes... I'm intrigued....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T19:26:40-08:00","id":844869,"title":"","content":"You say that as if politicians in CoD aren't supernaturals (or puppet mastered by them) already","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T19:36:40-08:00","id":844872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844869#post844869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say that as if politicians in CoD aren't supernaturals (or puppet mastered by them) already</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it adds to the horror if most politicians are just humans :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T02:51:17-08:00","id":844989,"title":"","content":"One thing to keep in mind, when talking about the wider CofD, is that tier 3 games like Mage and Mummy have influence on national politics. Tier 1 and 2 games have fingers in all manner of local government. That implies that, yeah, puppet masters. Especially when we talk about the Union Ministry. &quot;Just human&quot; is becoming vanishing small as more games come out. How many monster-related killers do we get (Huntsman, Slashers, Strix, Hosts, etc) before we eclipse the human murder rate in so many places?<br /> <br /> One of the conceits of the CofD is that magic touches virtually every life, but few believe it (the Lie, God Machine protocols, etc). Just human without a spirit Urging, vampire neighbor, or whatever seems to be the exception instead of rule. Not saying it can't happen, but odds are surprisingly against it, and only getting worse. With Deviant, we're hitting corrupt Big Business next, and that is on top of Mammon, Daeva Corp, the Tokyo one, and whatever the Mummy one is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T03:53:17-08:00","id":844997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844836#post844836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Food for thought. Beasts seem to be the only splat without a &amp;quot;human&amp;quot; end-game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the werewolves would disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T04:08:07-08:00","id":845004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=844997#post844997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the werewolves would disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>And demon, geist, and (I think) mage.<br /> <br /> ... Geist does get close... but killing your geist leaves you pretty inhuman with how torn up your soul is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T04:25:15-08:00","id":845009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=845004#post845004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And demon, geist, and (I think) mage.<br /> <br /> ... Geist does get close... but killing your geist leaves you pretty inhuman with how torn up your soul is.</div> </div> </div> </div> You forgot Changeling. But Geist does have a human end-game. You can actually resolve your Geister's anchors and unfinished business, and have them move on and revert to being human again. Its not highly detailed, but it is mentioned in a place or two.<br /> <br /> But, yeah. Lots of games without a human end-game. Vampires technically do have that possibilty with Transcendance / Golconda, but that's really fading more and more into the background as a left over of Masquerade. Werewolves don't touch on becoming human again, mage doesn't, changelings are too proud of their scars. Poor demons - turns out that achieving Hell is really more of a pipe dream, and the G-M never really leaves you alone without some very extreme measures, like completely obliterating God (good luck) or moving to an alternative dimension and hope there's no Gears there. There is no happy end game for the demons. Though, it is notable that there is an Embed that makes you completely human for a scene.<br /> <br /> EDIT - for that matter? There is a &quot;virtually human&quot; option for Beasts as well. Simply hit Satiety 10. You lose your magical powers, your Beast goes to sleep. For all intents and purposes, you're a regular human at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-10-2016, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T04:31:02-08:00","id":845011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=845009#post845009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You forgot Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling now has a human endgame with 2e's playtest previews iirc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Geist does have a human end-game. You can actually resolve your Geister's anchors and unfinished business, and have them move on and revert to being human again. Its not highly detailed, but it is mentioned in a place or two. </div> </div> </div>... but isn't their last anchor their keystone which just recreates itself after an hour or two... How do you resolve the anchors of something that cast away all it's anchors and replaced them with keys turning itself into an eldritch abomination, except for it's last anchor which becomes indestructible @_@","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T04:43:34-08:00","id":845015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=845011#post845011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling now has a human endgame with 2e's playtest previews iirc.</div> </div> </div> </div> Huh. Missed that one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ... but isn't their last anchor their keystone which just recreates itself after an hour or two... How do you resolve the anchors of something that cast away all it's anchors and replaced them with keys turning itself into an eldritch abomination, except for it's last anchor which becomes indestructible @_@ </div> </div> </div> Anchors have never been clearly defined. By definition, ghosts in the Underworld are anchor-less; anchors tie ghosts to the living world. Ghosts become geister in the Underworld. Geister somehow have keystones, which are anchors? The entire thing is just a mess of confusion that breaks down if you try to understand it all in clearly defined aspects.<br /> <br /> Perhaps using the word &quot;issues&quot; might be better. You are basically resolving some unfinished business or emotions or whatever that tied the giester into becoming a ghost in the first place. Geister, while they have evolved into more powerful beings, are still ghosts at heart and can be freed to move on like any other ghost. The memory and time lapsed tend to be a problem, but its entirely doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T04:56:43-08:00","id":845018,"title":"","content":"If memory serves in 2E Geister are at the level where &quot;create anchor&quot; becomes a power they can use. So the keys and keystones might be an application of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T05:00:58-08:00","id":845021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=845015#post845015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anchors have never been clearly defined. By definition, ghosts in the Underworld are anchor-less; anchors tie ghosts to the living world. Ghosts become geister in the Underworld. Geister somehow have keystones, which are anchors? The entire thing is just a mess of confusion that breaks down if you try to understand it all in clearly defined aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I can tell, they go to the underworld, get deformed and altered and then there is a small chance one will find a way to reform their last anchor (since the last anchor becomes the geists keystone and also explains why the keystone just repairs itself and why the geist has an anchor despite having been to the underworld), aka &quot;found a way to break the laws of death that send ghosts screaming to the Underworld when their last anchor is destroyed&quot; and then after that they &quot;manage to replace its missing anchors with something else: something archetypal&quot; through taken on keys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T05:41:30-08:00","id":845032,"title":"","content":"But once an anchor reforms, they should be banned from the Underworld. Ghosts with anchors literally cannot entire the Underworld, even if they want to. Clearly, that's not the case with Geists. Keystones, despite being called an anchor, have nothing in common with actual anchor rules. They're just called it. Which brings me back to the whole naming convention issue.<br /> <br /> GtSE was designed to be a bare bones game, and when combined with the grab-bag metaphysics that (by the book itself) shouldn't work? Some of the metaphysicis aren't highly detailed and entirely left up to the ST to define. Which is entirely by design, I bet. GtSE is deliberately a bare bones game where you pretty much customize everything, from weaknesses to character abilities to style of stories. So that also kind of makes an entire discussion of GtSE metaphysics pointless, because there's too much that's customized.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T10:30:38-08:00","id":845157,"title":"","content":"A geist's issues can be resolved, a Sin-Eater can live without the affliction of the Vacant by doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T12:50:24-08:00","id":845217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=845032#post845032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But once an anchor reforms, they should be banned from the Underworld. Ghosts with anchors literally cannot entire the Underworld, even if they want to. Clearly, that's not the case with Geists. Keystones, despite being called an anchor, have nothing in common with actual anchor rules. They're just called it. Which brings me back to the whole naming convention issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is likely why they are basically all up in the mortal world with the few that are in the underworld being from people attached to sin-eaters they gave up on or geists who pasted through avernain gates. And I'm not sure how it doesn't work like an anchor since, it serves the same purpose as an anchor (the book specifical says it's a safeguard against being dragged into the underworld since if it has no anchors it gets dragged to the underworld like a ghost, which is exactly how 2e anchors work).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">GtSE was designed to be a bare bones game, and when combined with the grab-bag metaphysics that (by the book itself) shouldn't work? Some of the metaphysicis aren't highly detailed and entirely left up to the ST to define. Which is entirely by design, I bet. GtSE is deliberately a bare bones game where you pretty much customize everything, from weaknesses to character abilities to style of stories. So that also kind of makes an entire discussion of GtSE metaphysics pointless, because there's too much that's customized.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> Heh, those krewe mythology rules can make things difficult :P</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T20:50:33-08:00","id":845426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=845032#post845032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But once an anchor reforms, they should be banned from the Underworld. Ghosts with anchors literally cannot entire the Underworld, even if they want to. Clearly, that's not the case with Geists. Keystones, despite being called an anchor, have nothing in common with actual anchor rules. They're just called it. Which brings me back to the whole naming convention issue</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it specifically, &quot;If you have an anchor, you cannot <b>enter</b> the Underworld&quot;? Because that doesn't address the scenario of a ghost having no anchors, entering the Underworld, and then gaining an anchor on the other side, because they would have satisfied entering the Underworld while they had no anchors. Is there a statement that anchors cannot exist in the Underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T21:01:56-08:00","id":845433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=845426#post845426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it specifically, &quot;If you have an anchor, you cannot <b>enter</b> the Underworld&quot;? Because that doesn't address the scenario of a ghost having no anchors, entering the Underworld, and then gaining an anchor on the other side, because they would have satisfied entering the Underworld while they had no anchors. Is there a statement that anchors cannot exist in the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>1e's Underworld doesn't permit ghosts to enter the Underworld while they still have their anchors. (It's one of the bullet points Geist's Underworld appendix covers in its summary of how ghosts work there.) 2e's ghost mechanics still have an equivalent of 1e's anchors in the form of the instances of a ghost's Anchor Condition that are instantiated with its genesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T05:55:44-08:00","id":845579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=845433#post845433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e's Underworld doesn't permit ghosts to enter the Underworld while they still have their anchors. (It's one of the bullet points Geist's Underworld appendix covers in its summary of how ghosts work there.) 2e's ghost mechanics still have an equivalent of 1e's anchors in the form of the instances of a ghost's Anchor Condition that are instantiated with its genesis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It seems like this old rule might have been discarded for the new edition of CofD because (if my memory is serving me correctly) only Rank 1 and 2 ghosts naturally occur outside of the Underworld and it seems rather unlikely that higher ranked ghosts don't or wouldn't have anchors. There's a weird inconsistency if we assume both the CofD (2e) rules and the Geist 1.1e rules are correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T07:11:10-08:00","id":845619,"title":"","content":"Rank 3+ ghosts lack anchors because generally losing all your anchors is <i>required</i> to become a rank 3+ ghost. They had them originally. Then they lost them. Then they got powerful.<br /> <br /> You can't make an anchor in the underworld because it wouldn't be an anchor. Those are specifically things tying you to the mortal world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-11-2016, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T08:45:18-08:00","id":845662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=845619#post845619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rank 3+ ghosts lack anchors because generally losing all your anchors is <i>required</i> to become a rank 3+ ghost. They had them originally. Then they lost them. Then they got powerful.<br /> <br /> You can't make an anchor in the underworld because it wouldn't be an anchor. Those are specifically things tying you to the mortal world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, once a Rank 4+ ghost <i>does</i> get summoned to the living world, they can use their Influence to <i>create</i> Anchors. They'll need to do stuff to freeze the Condition, by they can, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T09:31:50-08:00","id":845678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=845662#post845662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, once a Rank 4+ ghost <i>does</i> get summoned to the living world, they can use their Influence to <i>create</i> Anchors. They'll need to do stuff to freeze the Condition, by they can, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div> If circumstances allow, they could contract a Gravetouched Changeling to do their work for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:08:19-08:00","id":845731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=845433#post845433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e's Underworld doesn't permit ghosts to enter the Underworld while they still have their anchors. (It's one of the bullet points Geist's Underworld appendix covers in its summary of how ghosts work there.) 2e's ghost mechanics still have an equivalent of 1e's anchors in the form of the instances of a ghost's Anchor Condition that are instantiated with its genesis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But that's to <b>enter</b> the Underworld. How does that matter if you're discussing a Ghost that's already <b>in</b> the Underworld and gains an Anchor? Is there a specific mention that Ghosts cannot have Anchors inside the Underworld, or is there merely mention that crossing the boundary into the Underworld (a single direction scenario as that doesn't address <b>leaving</b> the Underworld with or without an Anchor)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:19:34-08:00","id":845736,"title":"","content":"Behold! I have driven my own thread into an unrelated tangent! Muhhahahhahahahahaha!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T11:26:18-08:00","id":845739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=845736#post845736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Behold! I have driven my own thread into an unrelated tangent! Muhhahahhahahahahaha!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3eICovmVyAU\" data-code=\"3eICovmVyAU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/3eICovmVyAU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T21:42:58-08:00","id":845947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/842010-beasts-overpowered-try-underpowered?p=845731#post845731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's to <b>enter</b> the Underworld. How does that matter if you're discussing a Ghost that's already <b>in</b> the Underworld and gains an Anchor?</div> </div> </div> </div>The aggregate of incidental dev comments suggest that the answer to the underlying discussion that is not the tangentially-related question that I answered at goddamn midnight is that Bound Geists Are Weird And/Or Not Entirely What They Seem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there a specific mention that Ghosts cannot have Anchors inside the Underworld, or is there merely mention that crossing the boundary into the Underworld (a single direction scenario as that doesn't address <b>leaving</b> the Underworld with or without an Anchor)? </div> </div> </div>That is a scenario that literally does not happen without outside intervention and, by the mechanics of 2e available so far, only matters if the ghost comes out of the Underworld to a place that has temporarily gained a new Anchor Condition tagged to it and suspends the duration of that Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T16:23:05-07:00","id":851432,"title":"","content":"Another area that Beasts are good at is healing and reducing damage. Besides all those Immunities they accumulate via Atavisms and Lair Traits, they also have an unique healing method as part of their template. They can spend 1 Satiety to heal 1 aggravated damage or all bashing damage. They must be in their Lairs to do so, but since they can spend willpower points instead of Satiety to improve Atavisms while in the Lair, you can say that they can heal aggravated and bashing damage with willpower points too. If they have Unbreakable, Relentless Hunter and Iron Skin, they become even harder to take down. This isn't on the same level as the different types of Regeneration that werewolves have (especially in Gauru form), but it is still impressive. They only have so many Satiety and willpower points, though, and regaining Satiety takes more time than 